ode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1431773#post1431773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Cockscomb Society is such a glow up on the original, especially the bane. I think that'll be my next preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I had a lot of fun writing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T19:25:13-08:00","id":1431779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1431765#post1431765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While this book is really full of good stuff (just keep that parasite awaty from me, please), my two favorites are the Nowhere Men and the Noctuku Strain. I really like the Noctuku in this form (I prefer it over the original bloodline format, actually), and I kinda like to think about it as the Nosferatu's version of Malkavia (even though that throwing it together witht he Contagion also works, but that also works for Malkavia, so...).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really happy to hear you like our take on the Noctuku. That was something the writer and I had a lot of back and forth about. Originally, we were going to present them as a corrupted bloodline, but then he added in a sidebar about them being a disease, and we both were like &quot;Oh, that's way better.&quot;<br /> <br /> And the Nowhere Men are one of those weird things I love finding in Night Horrors book. The author (same as the Noctuku) created a really neat little plot hook you can throw at your Nosferatu and Mekhet; they're kind of making up for only having one Horror in Strange Shades. I'm glad you liked them and their weird Obfuscate interplay. As a matter of fact, all three of the Horrors map to a Haunt Discipline, thematically if not literally.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;living&quot; Disciplines and Malkavia and the like... well, [REDACTED].<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T23:24:36-08:00","id":1431799,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I'm terrible at self-promotion and forgot to post this. Follow us here:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/nonedarker\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://facebook.com/security/hsts-pixel.gif?c=3.2.5\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/nonedarker\" target=\"_blank\"> Log in or sign up to view </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/nonedarker\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.facebook.com/nonedarker </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> See posts, photos and more on Facebook. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T12:23:54-08:00","id":1431857,"title":"","content":"Another preview this Monday afternoon, this time the Cockscomb Society, by our very own <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a>. The Cockerels first appeared in <b>The Beast That Haunts the Blood: Nosferatu</b>, one of two bloodlines from the book, the other being the Lygos. We'll get to the Lygos tomorrow, but for now, have a look at what's new with the elite of Clan Nosferatu:<br /> <br /> <b>The Cockscomb Society: The Ones Who Could Buy and Sell You<br /> <br /> &quot;That face of yours is just priceless. Well... almost.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cHe cleans up nicely, doesn\u2019t he?\u201d they whisper when they think he isn\u2019t listening.<br /> <br /> \u201cFor a Nosferatu. Such a shame he wasn\u2019t Embraced by someone with better breeding.\u201d<br /> <br /> He\u2019s used to backhanded praise. It\u2019s the story they need to tell themselves to explain how a lowly Haunt could climb so far above them on the social ladder.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou don\u2019t think it\u2019s true, do you? The awful things they say he gets up to behind closed doors\u2026 I can\u2019t imagine.\u201d<br /> <br /> It is true, of course. Everything they\u2019ve heard and more. He makes no apologies for playing the game better than they ever could, but he would never advertise his\u2026 indiscretions.<br /> <br /> Bad taste, that.</i><br /> <br /> The Nosferatu have a reputation for flaunting their monstrosity. Their curse is impossible to conceal, so why not wear it with pride? Not so for the Cockscomb Society. They may be frightening, but that shouldn\u2019t mean they abandon all sense of propriety. More so even than other, more \u201cpresentable\u201d Kindred, Ladies and Gents of the Society practice the Masquerade with a dogmatic ardor. They rehearse every step of the Danse Macabre until they can walk it in their daysleep. They have little choice, as anything less would belie their station as one of the most well-to-do lineages in the All Night Society.<br /> <br /> Founded in the late 18th century, the Cockscomb Society climbed the social ladder with alarming speed, and they\u2019ve remained at the top ever since. Their founder, Potter Woolsthorpe Wycombe, accomplished this by rejecting the insularity of his clan and immersing himself in human high society. Forging countless relationships with the rich and powerful, he pulled himself out of the Necropolis by his own bootstraps. So what if a few moral compromises had to be made along the way? That\u2019s the cost of building a legacy.<br /> <br /> It began with revenants. Reasoning these undesirables wouldn\u2019t be missed among the Kindred, Wycombe scoured the Warrens for cast-off victims and failed Embraces. Using the resources he\u2019d accumulated from his mortal pawns, he provided orphaned vampires with just enough blood to keep their hunger at bay. Then, once they were dependent on him for survival, he sold them to wealthy mortals belonging to the most infamous Hellfire Club in the world: Ashwood Abbey, notorious for visiting all manner of depraved abuses upon captive vampires, among other exotic victims.<br /> <br /> For a time, this was a profitable endeavor, but the Abbey\u2019s appetite for dead flesh was nigh infinite. As demand grew, Wycombe began uplifting followers from among his captives, gradually expanding his operation to keep up with the developing market. Soon, revenants alone weren\u2019t enough. Buyers wanted more dangerous toys, and before long Wycombe and his uplifted childer began Embracing hapless mortals directly into their chattel. Finally, the disappearances became too much for the local court to ignore, and Wycombe\u2019s operations were shut down. However, by this time, Wycombe\u2019s brood and their fortune had grown so large that they had secured their place as indispensable members of the Kindred ruling class.<br /> <br /> Tonight, Wycombe\u2019s descendants struggle to escape the shadow of their progenitors\u2019 crimes, while still enjoying their long-term benefits. Of course, the Cockscomb Society no longer engages in such untoward business practices, but the reputation hangs over its members like bad English weather. The Society\u2019s commitment to decorum and politesse is therefore a social necessity, not only to disprove assumptions other Kindred make based on their clan, but also to dispel any suspicion they may also be guilty of their grandsire\u2019s improprieties. They wouldn\u2019t be caught dead otherwise.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> You don\u2019t want to wallow in your monstrosity like the others. You aren\u2019t proud of being a freak, but you\u2019re not about to let it hold you back. You recognize your curse for what it is, but you\u2019re prepared to take it in stride, and still put everyone else to shame. The others may sneer and whisper behind your back, but who cares what they think when you have more connections than the harpies, more blood dolls than the prince, and more money than God?<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> We have our finger on the pulse of the herd. We\u2019re closer to the kine than anyone else, and we control the flow of the most valuable resource there is\u2026 cash. You weren\u2019t expecting that, were you? Be honest, you thought I was going to say blood. Typical. See, that\u2019s what separates us from the other Haunts. We recognize the value in material wealth. Spooky powers and disappearing acts are cute and all, but money can alter the course of history in ways even elders could never dream.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s no secret we got where we are because of the awful things our founder did. We all carry that with us. We all benefit from his crimes, and it would be so easy to fall into the same trap he did. Wycombe may be a monster, but he did what he did so you could have a better Requiem than he ever had. Can you honestly say you wouldn\u2019t have done the same in his position? What would you be willing to do to hold on to the privileges his indiscretions bought you? What wouldn\u2019t you be willing to do to insure your own childer and grandchilder can enjoy the same advantages you have?<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Origins (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> In the depths of the Roman Necropolis, an owl swallowed a worm. The worm wriggled in its gullet, struggling against its fate, until the bird could take it no more. It expelled the contents of its gut, and out of the pellet crawled the half-digested remains of what had once been the worm, alive, but changed. The worm carried something of its devourer with it, which it passed onto its spawn. For countless generations, the worm\u2019s brood harbored a hunger no loam could sate, for theirs was the appetite of a raptor. But the worms suffered in their famine, for they knew nothing else. Until one night, a rooster ate one of these tainted worms. At last, this avian hunger had found its way home. Now that same hunger lives on in the bellies of the Cockerels, as it was always meant to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 01-12-2021, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T22:16:10-08:00","id":1431920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1431765#post1431765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While this book is really full of good stuff (just keep that parasite awaty from me, please), my two favorites are the Nowhere Men and the Noctuku Strain. I really like the Noctuku in this form (I prefer it over the original bloodline format, actually), and I kinda like to think about it as the Nosferatu's version of Malkavia (even though that throwing it together witht he Contagion also works, but that also works for Malkavia, so...). That kinda makes me think about what could be the other parallels for the rest of the Clans- even though that doing it simply for symmetry's sake could downgrade the mystery behind it a bit. As for the Nowhere Men, they really give the feeling of Discipline Mysticism and the feeling of &quot;living Disciplines&quot;- either meaning that Obfuscate connects to something <i>other</i> (which have implications for the origin of the Disciplines and how they work- as if Obfuscate is &quot;the Place Beyond the Fire&quot;, and the strix are basically smoke and shadows, and then you do 2 + 2 and get that maybe by cloaking them with Obfuscate the vampires remove themselves to the so called Dis- which ties those things to the strix and I could go on and on with those implications), or that Obfuscate is <i>alive, </i>and the Nowhere Men are its incarnations which are very, very hungry- and that maybe other Disciplines also have other incarnations (which once agains goes to tying them to the strix because vampires and embodied entities and such).<br /> <br /> Inn short, it is all very cool. I'll leave a review once the site would let me do so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Concerning the other Clans, I can't help but think that the Gangrel's depravations would not come from an over-abundance of the Beast but rather its sleepiness. What would take it place as it slumber but the Gangrel has to feed and deal with his mutable undead body without the reassuring presence of his Beast? To which depth would he fall simply to reawaken it ? That could be interesting to explore I think.<br /> <br /> Also, this book seems awesome ! I don't have much money right now but when i'll have, I think I'll add it to my collection <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 01-12-2021, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T22:50:49-08:00","id":1431923,"title":"","content":"I will say this book (and its sibling Strange Shade) was great! Its been a while since I devoured a source book as quickly and made me want to read me more while sparking tons of &quot;Oh wow that's cool what if-&quot; moments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12824-bloodyquill","name":"Bloodyquill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T10:55:24-08:00","id":1431982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bloodyquill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1431923#post1431923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say this book (and its sibling Strange Shade) was great! Its been a while since I devoured a source book as quickly and made me want to read me more while sparking tons of &amp;quot;Oh wow that's cool what if-&amp;quot; moments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait till you see the next one!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T11:45:55-08:00","id":1431989,"title":"","content":"Oh wow, already? <i>Nice.</i> Cannot wait to get my hands on this! In particular, I'm very interested in what this team has done with necropoli, since I find the 1e mechanics really... I just don't like them. So I'm looking forward to what everyone here has done, especially since my previous attempts to hack necropoli haven't really satisfied me. |D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T14:19:39-08:00","id":1432005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1431989#post1431989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh wow, already? <i>Nice.</i> Cannot wait to get my hands on this! In particular, I'm very interested in what this team has done with necropoli, since I find the 1e mechanics really... I just don't like them. So I'm looking forward to what everyone here has done, especially since my previous attempts to hack necropoli haven't really satisfied me. |D</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly enough, we took some inspiration from the mechanics for lodges in <b>Werewolf</b>. Obviously, Necropoli don't have totems or sacred hunts, but we were able to take the bare bones of that system and turn it into something creepy and thematic (with a few twists). Warrens are more oriented for all-Haunt chronicles, but the material there has lots of things you could use in a regular chronicle. And the sample Necropoli are some of my favorite things in the book.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Necropoli, that brings us to today's preview: The Lygos.<br /> <br /> The Lygos are the other bloodline from <b>The Beast That Haunts the Blood</b>, and, honestly, they're the less interesting of the pair, in my opinion. They're kind of a retread of the Baddacelli from <b>Bloodlines: The Chosen</b>, without any cool sound powers. So, while you'll certainly recognize them, they've gotten a little stranger over the years...<br /> <br /> <b>Lygos: The Ones Who Snuff Out Your Light</b><br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Don't be silly. Of course you should be afraid of the dark.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Children fear the dark. In some, this phobia is fleeting, easily dismissed with a moment\u2019s thought. In others, it lingers for years, requiring constant reassurance and parental comfort. Yet when these children grow up, they\u2019re expected to just get over it. Put away the night-light; pull the blanket down. Most people manage to rationalize away their juvenile fears, but some never do, panicking in unlit rooms well into adulthood.<br /> <br /> Why is that? Why do some people never get over an irrational fear of the dark?<br /> <br /> Maybe because they know it\u2019s not irrational. On a primal level, they know that the things they hid from in childish terror weren\u2019t imaginary. That they\u2019re real. That they have a name.<br /> <br /> The Lygos are an ancient line, dating back to before true cities sprouted over the world\u2019s surface. They dwelled in places the sun never touched, dragging victims down where none could hear their screams. When other, lesser Nosferatu rose to the surface to scratch out a meager existence in the light, the Lygos remained below, as all Kindred should. They learned to listen to the dark, to hear its secrets, and let it guide them to beings that had never known the light, more wonderful and terrible than any vampire. The Lygos came to serve them, these Dwellers Below, and in exchange they gifted the Truths of Erebus upon them, so they might better cleave to their masters.<br /> <br /> Rumors cling to the Lygos like wet earth. An Acolyte from Bucharest says they devour light like other Kindred consume blood. A Dragon in Istanbul claims they have no hearts, just chunks of obsidian embedded beneath their ribs. However, no matter how strange the rumor, all stories of the Lygos have a commonality: They hate the light. Lygos have been caught sabotaging streetlights, snuffing candles, shattering flashlights, and otherwise destroying any light-source they can get their hands on, even inactive ones. These Kindred don\u2019t just inhabit and encourage the dark \u2014 they worship it. Other vampires often hear them uttering prayers as they knock over lampposts or smash lightbulbs, as if birthing shadow were a holy act.<br /> <br /> Due to this obsession, most Lygos live underground. Not content with boarded windows and blackout curtains, a Creep won\u2019t sleep soundly without a few feet of dirt between her and the sun. It takes extreme circumstances for a Shade to accept a haven above ground, and if nothing suitable is available, she\u2019ll make her own, burrowing deep beneath the earth with her own two hands. The Lygos are proficient Necropoli builders, and almost never emerge from their tunnels except to feed, or to carry out their bizarre work.<br /> <br /> The Shades are content to let the Kindred whisper; what the All Night Society thinks has never mattered to them. The Lygos know the truth, after all. If they extinguish enough light, and spread the righteous fear of the dark, their masters will rise from the deepest places in the earth, covering the world in blissful blackness. They do this not just for themselves, but for the sake of all vampires. One night soon, they\u2019ll thank the Lygos. The Shades know the world began in darkness, and in the end, that\u2019s all that will be left.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> You exist in a world of perpetual night, so why not command the darkness? You find the dark comforting and know it\u2019s where you really belong. You\u2019re tired of those in the world above calling your appearance offensive, or your actions strange. Here in the void, no one can judge you.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> Other Kindred cling to the edges of light, but only we make the darkness our skin. There is nowhere you can run from us, because night is our ally. There is nowhere you can hide from us, because we are the shadows where you seek shelter. There is nowhere you can escape from us, because light is just an imposition. Darkness is the natural state.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> Ours is a losing war. Every day the kine fill the world with more light, soiling the purity of darkness. Few places are truly dark, yet our masters compel us to make more. We fear disappointing them \u2014 even more than the light, and our zeal blinds us in ways it never could.<br /> <br /> <b>The Truths of Erebus (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> The Dwellers Below taught the Shades much, and the bloodline\u2019s elders have codified and spread these lessons so all Lygos might benefit from their wisdom. These are the Truths of Erebus. Similar to a Coil of the Dragon, the Truths bring about personal transformation, but rather than overcoming the Kindred Curse, the Truths adapt the Lygos to a Requiem in the deep darkness, making them more akin to the things they serve.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lidless Eye \u2022</b><br /> <br /> If everything is darkness, then nothing is, and \u201cnothing\u201d provides no barrier to sight. The vampire can see perfectly in total darkness, ignoring all situational penalties and Tilts like Blinded. Nothing can obscure her sight \u2014 not even the destruction of her eyes. Furthermore, she becomes attuned to the low places of the world, adding her Truths dots to Blood Potency for the purposes of Kindred Senses when moving through darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T20:55:58-08:00","id":1432044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1432005#post1432005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interestingly enough, we took some inspiration from the mechanics for lodges in <b>Werewolf</b>. Obviously, Necropoli don't have totems or sacred hunts, but we were able to take the bare bones of that system and turn it into something creepy and thematic (with a few twists). Warrens are more oriented for all-Haunt chronicles, but the material there has lots of things you could use in a regular chronicle. And the sample Necropoli are some of my favorite things in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot of sense, tbh. The Lodge Merits are basically a more streamlined version of the shared Merit pool used to construct necropoli in 1e, so giving those Merits a Lodgey makeover is really obvious in retrospect!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T21:25:09-08:00","id":1432045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1432044#post1432044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That makes a lot of sense, tbh. The Lodge Merits are basically a more streamlined version of the shared Merit pool used to construct necropoli in 1e, so giving those Merits a Lodgey makeover is really obvious in retrospect!</div> </div> </div> </div>That may in fact have been what went through my mind. \u201cOh, these are like lodge Merits!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T00:55:01-08:00","id":1432051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1432045#post1432045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That may in fact have been what went through my mind. \u201cOh, these are like lodge Merits!\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that also nicely addresses one of my biggest complaints about the 1e system. There isn't a complex system of individual Merits providing semi-universal benefits to everyone, or rather there is, but it is fake, and you don't lose access to the library if Sneaky Pete meets the sun, or whatever. You also have to opt-in on the effects you want, rather than buying an entrance fee Merit so you can use the goodies of some NPC that you were really after.<br /> <br /> I like this a lot. Even more excited to get my hands on it, now!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T13:14:14-08:00","id":1432113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1432051#post1432051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, that also nicely addresses one of my biggest complaints about the 1e system. There isn't a complex system of individual Merits providing semi-universal benefits to everyone, or rather there is, but it is fake, and you don't lose access to the library if Sneaky Pete meets the sun, or whatever. You also have to opt-in on the effects you want, rather than buying an entrance fee Merit so you can use the goodies of some NPC that you were really after.<br /> <br /> I like this a lot. Even more excited to get my hands on it, now!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the original mechanics struck me as trying to do a lot with a little. It's a neat idea, but we felt it needed a more robust system. That being said, we tried to make sure the Merits we included could be used in regular play without the entire Necropolis system. You could even use Clots (the hazardous environmental &quot;quirks&quot; that pop up in Warrens) without any of the other stuff.<br /> <br /> But yes, I hope you enjoy it!<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's our next preview.<br /> <br /> unLike some of the other updated bloodlines, our Yagnatia aren't too different in outlook or aesthetics, but of the four older bloodlines, they're the ones who've changed the most mechanically. I liked their old bane, but while the idea of the infertile bite has some interesting story hooks to it, I wanted that to be a family custom rather than an inherent thing. Conclusion being, it felt a bit too passive for a bane in Second Edition, though their original weakness is included as an optional system, and we present an option so both versions could exist in your chronicle. I also felt that, unlike other Haunts, the Yagnatia wouldn't have much interest in skulking through the shadows, so their Disciplines have been tweaked as well. Now they favor Resilience over Obfuscate. I just really love Haunts with Resilience <i>and </i>Vigor. It wasn't an arbitrary decision, of course, but you'll have to read their entry to see why.<br /> <br /> <b>Yagnatia: The Ones Who Rule You<br /> <br /> &quot;My crown is my blood, and my blood is the birthright of my gods.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> He carries himself in the manner of one born with a silver spoon in his mouth, but the too-wide grin suggests a dagger. The blood beneath his fingernails is fresh with the scent of copper, yet he still expects you to wipe your boots before you step into his parlor. Mind the carpet! It hasn\u2019t been fed. When he invites you to stay for dinner, you\u2019re not sure whether to be frightened or flattered. A little of both eases digestion, they say, but answer quick lest your host be offended. Answer quick or you\u2019ll be the silverware.<br /> <br /> The Yagnatia defy their clan\u2019s lot in the Danse Macabre. Most Haunts are self-loathing serfs who fear their own faces, and wouldn\u2019t know power if it staked them through a throne. But to a Boyar, horror is divine right. Wearing her clan\u2019s curse on a velvet sleeve just means she\u2019s more fit to rule.<br /> <br /> This regal terror isn\u2019t just temporal power. It\u2019s spiritual. Witch-Kings and Sorcerer-Queens, the old gods of Russia blessed the Yagnatia as they rose to rule the Dark Ages, and so they reign their fiefs with a wormwood wand, not a scepter. Before the Circle of Crone spread like a parasite across the Old World, the Boyars knew the secrets of Cr\u00faac, holding the night against Westerners set on tearing down pagan ways. The Lancea et Sanctum and Clan Ventrue \u2014 pretenders to imperial legacies they themselves destroyed \u2014 were the bloodline\u2019s undying foes in a war for the Russian nightlife, and the Yagnatia still bear those grudges with a bitter glee.<br /> <br /> The Boyar will to power takes many forms. They lair in both fortified manses and high-security skyscrapers, content to shepherd their vassals away from corruption and quaint ideas like democracy. Some are warlords cum wizards, commanding dead armies fat on the ichor of dark gods, while others play the stock market with spiritual insider trading. However they choose to spend their Requiems, the Yagnatia value a strict caste system above all else. Those born above remain above, and those below should remember their manners.<br /> <br /> Yet, for all their fealty to tradition, the Yagnatia have few holdings left in the Motherland. As the centuries wore on, the Sanctified won the souls of Russian Kindred, and the Ventrue won their minds, but the death blow came when the Bolsheviks seized power. In a frenzy of Embraces, the bloodline\u2019s enemies commanded their fledglings to topple \u201ctsarist\u201d Yagnatia domains, sweeping away their wealth, their faith, and their death grip on feudalism. Following the civil war, the Boyars scattered. Some remained in their ancestral land, but more than half fled to Western Europe and East Asia. Many feared this would break the bloodline\u2019s link to the land, but the Yagnatia are nothing if not adaptable. Most found new spirits in new environs, and new gods to legitimize their rule.<br /> <br /> The Boyars keep their numbers small. Only those of noble heritage may join the bloodline, though in recent years they\u2019ve begun to welcome more non-Slavs. However, a Yagnatia never Embraces without permission from her titled elders, and this practice has led to rumors of impotent Vitae \u2014 rumors the Yagnatia themselves spread among their rivals, spinning tales of witches and an infertile bite.<br /> <br /> Better the Kindred believe they could never rise again.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> Would you rather be a tunnel grub or command men with an awful glance? We chose the latter, and thus we became the chosen in turn. We are beloved of the gods, and so they allowed us to remake them to better fit our needs. You need only look upon our faces to see their blessings. Few are worthy of our Vitae, but those who are become more than sniveling Haunts.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> Humans have such limited philosophies. This is true of the lower classes as well (both living and dead), but humans\u2026 humans cling to the silly belief that they\u2019re owed something for being alive. That they deserve life. The gods are not so generous. We teach the low that life must be earned, and remind the high that the gods can always choose to take it away \u2014 and that we are the instrument of that choice.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> We could be wrong. Maybe we\u2019re just like all the other rats, but managed to upholster our garbage. What happens when everyone else realizes it? What happens when the spirits we command by the grace of our gods see it\u2019s all a pretense, and that we\u2019re just blood-sacks playing at nobility with forces we don\u2019t really understand?<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan:</b> Nosferatu<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Boyars, Vozhds, Pretenders (post-1917; disrespectful)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Curse of Bielobog):</b> The Boyars honor the gods of the land, and they must answer for all disrespect. A Yagnatia\u2019s Humanity caps any dice pools or traits used to resist the Numina of ephemeral beings. This also applies to Strix Dread Powers and Embodiments.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> <i>Dominate</i>, <i>Nightmare</i>, Resilience, Vigor","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 01-13-2021, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T15:56:26-08:00","id":1432137,"title":"","content":"I got it. And I love it - it really nails how Nosferatu are both the most inhuman and most humane Clan; the monster is obvious, but that's because it's most distinct from the Man in Haunts. They know exactly what the source of their problems are, and they revel in and curse it in equal measure. A Nosferatu's most lethal secret is shown for the world to see - they don't have as much to hide, so often, you can trust them more - <i>if </i>they trust you first.<br /> <br /> Also, you really showed your creativity with the three Antagonists; Fear Eaters are rather admirable in their own way, even if they are a cult, Noctuku are some of the most creative takes on fear of zombies I've seen (they <i>can </i>infect Haunts, but the real risk is that they don't become brainless - they're <i>hunters), </i>and the Nowhere Men are incredible set dressing with an undertone of cosmic horror (after all - you can't kill them, you just see them long enough for them to make off with a hand).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T16:28:40-08:00","id":1432139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1432137#post1432137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got it. And I love it - it really nails how Nosferatu are both the most inhuman and most humane Clan; the monster is obvious, but that's because it's most distinct from the Man in Haunts. They know exactly what the source of their problems are, and they revel in and curse it in equal measure. A Nosferatu's most lethal secret is shown for the world to see - they don't have as much to hide, so often, you can trust them more - <i>if </i>they trust you first.<br /> <br /> Also, you really showed your creativity with the three Antagonists; Fear Eaters are rather admirable in their own way, even if they are a cult, Noctuku are some of the most creative takes on fear of zombies I've seen (they <i>can </i>infect Haunts, but the real risk is that they don't become brainless - they're <i>hunters), </i>and the Nowhere Men are incredible set dressing with an undertone of cosmic horror (after all - you can't kill them, you just see them long enough for them to make off with a hand).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much! That duality was a theme I wanted to hit hard in this one. The dirty cycle of being a Nosferatu is such a fun concept to play with, and I think all the writers nailed it.<br /> <br /> And I'll pass on your praise about the antagonists to their author. He spilled a lot of ink over them, and I think they worked out wonderfully. I'm especially fond of the Fear Eaters, because they're not the kind of antagonist you see much in <b>Vampire</b>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T09:34:04-08:00","id":1432209,"title":"","content":"Excellent work, just like with the last one!<br /> Just a question about authorial intent here. Most of the larger Bloodline Discipline adjustments make sense, like the Gethsemani trading in Vigor for Resilience or Yagnatia losing Obfuscate for Resilience, but I am not so clear on the logic of why the Keepers of the Dark also trade Vigor for Resilience. Any input you can give me here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T10:02:13-08:00","id":1432215,"title":"","content":"ChoD: Chcago still exists? I was surethis setting is first edition exclusively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 01-14-2021, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T10:11:33-08:00","id":1432217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1432215#post1432215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ChoD: Chcago still exists? I was surethis setting is first edition exclusively.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have not had much on Chicago in 2e, but we have had at least one new story about Maxwell and Birch in the Strix Chronicle Anthology, which also delves into the mystery of Old John. However, I do not remember any Chicago perspectives from the Idigam Chronicle and Fallen World Chronicle Anthologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":". 01-14-2021, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T10:37:03-08:00","id":1432222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1432209#post1432209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent work, just like with the last one!<br /> Just a question about authorial intent here. Most of the larger Bloodline Discipline adjustments make sense, like the Gethsemani trading in Vigor for Resilience or Yagnatia losing Obfuscate for Resilience, but I am not so clear on the logic of why the Keepers of the Dark also trade Vigor for Resilience. Any input you can give me here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you enjoy it!<br /> <br /> The Keepers are all about defense and opposition, less about fighting their enemies directly. They just make sure to survive long enough to bring the other guy down. They\u2019re also (not so secretly) the Lygos\u2019 eternal foes, and it makes sense for them to have opposing physical Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T10:41:51-08:00","id":1432224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1432215#post1432215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ChoD: Chcago still exists? I was surethis setting is first edition exclusively.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to what saibot said, Scratch has a whole backstory described in <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b>. And settings aren\u2019t really exclusive to editions, I\u2019d contend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T14:29:13-08:00","id":1432252,"title":"","content":"What's that you say? A preview? Why not!<br /> <br /> The Acteius are one of four new lineages in the book. However, their name HAS appeared in an official source! They're one of the bloodlines mentioned but never expanded on in <b>Vampire: The Requiem </b>(the very first one). I did a little research on the name, and while there were a few angles I could have come at them from, this one was what interested me most.<br /> <br /> <b>Acteius: The Ones You Can't Stop<br /> <br /> &quot;The hammer's not just for nails.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> The Kindred look down on the Nosferatu. Safe in timeless perfection, the others dismiss the Haunts as lessers, menials, or just plain goons. That stereotype is the knifepoint of an ageless prejudice \u2014 but it doesn\u2019t mean Haunts never take pride in their labor. Honest work, they call it, untainted by the power plays rotting the All Night Society. Look at a Nosferatu and you know what you get. The boils hide few secrets, and the acid terror crawling up your throat is nothing if not sincere. That doesn\u2019t make Nosferatu more trustworthy than other vampires, but they have few illusions.<br /> <br /> The Acteius subscribe to this view, and they\u2019ll defend it with a clawhammer. Tinkers, tailors, and anything in between, their workshops operate under a simple principle: The dead don\u2019t rest. Unbound from human wear and tear, the Embrace molds the Artisans into ceaseless machines of labor. See their skin crack off in the heat of the forge. Smell the iron as their fingers split on countless needle pricks. Work them to the bone \u2014 literally. You\u2019ll hear no complaints. With the art of Bloodcrafting, the Artisans warp stolen life into gory and glorious wonders, with mortal victims as the means of production. 3D printers before humans ever dreamed the concept, the Acteius were the backbone of Kindred armies and merchants for hundreds of years, spinning blood into swords and plowshares alike. Legend has it they smelted the crown of the Invictus Emperor, and some say their guilds defined the early Carthian Movement.<br /> <br /> Artisans take many jobs in many places, from sweat-drenched factory floors to the chilly halls of haute couture: Toiling beneath a dead assembly plant, a smith forges arms for a revolution, carving the prince\u2019s name on each shell case; atop the tallest skyscraper of the city\u2019s wealthiest block, a seamstress watches from a shadow veil as courtiers fawn over her fashions, shunning those she didn\u2019t deem worthy of her wares.<br /> <br /> Yet for all their talents, tonight, the Acteius are rare. Once, no one worked without their say in many domains. The trades weren\u2019t a hard market to corner among the dead, but the quality of their labor (and their method of \u201chandling\u201d competition) was unsurpassed. That is, until they started disappearing. Over the course of a hundred years, wherever Artisans made their havens, they fell through the cracks. Elders abandoned centuries-long projects, and whole coteries pulled up stakes without so much as a liquidation sale. A thousand rumors ran through the guildhalls, but if anyone had an inkling of the truth, they weren\u2019t sharing it. Worse, these disappearances outpaced the rate the bloodline could rebuild its ranks, as if each new Embrace or induction cost two Requiems. Without a way to communicate on a global scale, few realized the extent of the culling until it was much too late. In the end, all they had for it was a name: Doom.<br /> <br /> In the end, the Doom claimed three quarters of the bloodline. Only in the last 20 years have these disappearances ended, but the Artisans are still wary of spreading their Vitae too wide. A good builder always makes a few prototypes, and the Acteius fear they\u2019ve yet to see their enemy\u2019s final design.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> You want to create a spark of life without spawning a bloodsucking corpse. More than that, you want to take control. Other Nosferatu spend their Requiems looking for ways to stamp a bright side on ugly, but we don\u2019t need self-delusions to see us through the night. Maybe you can\u2019t hammer out what the Embrace did to your soul, but you can sure as fuck take it out on a scrap of metal.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> No one fights the assembly line. You can either get out of its way, or you can oil the tracks with your veins. Pay your bills and you won\u2019t hear any complaint from us, but fall behind on our fees? Exploit the working man? Well, then you\u2019ll make an excellent set of steak knives.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> You have to follow a schedule. You have to time things out, make habits, spreadsheets, invoices, five-year plans\u2026 all of which means jack shit if someone throws a spanner in the works. \u201cOrder\u201d and \u201cefficiency\u201d are just useful lies to tell yourself as the vein in your skull starts to pop. We can plan ahead all we like, but not for every eventuality, and if we didn\u2019t learn that after the last century, we never will.<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit: Bloodcrafting (\u2022\u2022+)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Acteius, Crafts \u2022\u2022\u2022, Specialty in Crafts<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Your character can create supernatural objects out of pure Vitae, appropriate to his Specialty in Crafts. He must buy this Merit again to use additional Specialties.<br /> <br /> To create a Bloodcraft, your character must spill his blood into an appropriate vessel (a forge, a sewing machine, a mold, etc.). By then spending a Willpower, he instills the blood with solidity and malleability, transforming it into whatever raw material he needs. Creating the final product requires an extended Dexterity + Crafts roll, with a base target of 10 successes. The interval is one roll per hour. If modifications add to the target number, necessary successes cannot exceed 20. If your character is interrupted, the blood reverts to normal, and he must begin again with a new batch.<br /> <br /> At its basic level, this Merit allows a vampire to create a simple object made of transfigured Vitae. The item will take on the qualities of a similar mundane object, and will pass cursory inspections, though materials like gems and precious metals will reveal themselves as fake to trained eyes. The object will always carry a hint of its true nature: a sword has a crimson sheen, while fabric made into a dress flows like blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-15T05:38:47-08:00","id":1432302,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to say that I started going through this book and the Mekhet book yesterday and I am enjoying them both immensely. I absolutely love the Chamenos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-15T12:05:11-08:00","id":1432329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1432302#post1432302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted to say that I started going through this book and the Mekhet book yesterday and I am enjoying them both immensely. I absolutely love the Chamenos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll let the writer know! The Chamenos are probably my favourite of the three ghoul families; they really exemplify the themes of the book.<br /> <br /> And now, a Friday excerpt. This time, let's visit the Von Schreck Family, purveyors of thrills, chills, and (allegedly) snuff films.<br /> <br /> <b>Von Schreck Family: The Ones Who Make You Scream<br /> <br /> &quot;Great, great, but this time, scream from the diaphragm. Action!&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Scary movies have a life of their own. If you ask historians, most will tell you the first horror film was <i>Le Manoir du Diable </i>(<i>The House of the Devil</i>) in 1896, or the 1910 adaptation of Frankenstein. A hundred years of horror have profoundly affected the human psyche. It\u2019s affected vampires too.<br /> <br /> The celebration of horror is a paradox. People love to be scared; in kind, they love <i>fear</i>. From this seeming contradiction, an odd bloodline of Nosferatu has emerged: The Von Schreck Family. Their progenitor, Hermann Von Schreck, attached himself to film projects as early as Edison, though the bloodline\u2019s real debut came in the 1960s, alongside schlocky horror fair for drive-ins and early chain theaters. Both monsters and heroines, the Scream Queens cemented themselves as elites of the genre. One by one, Hermann brought more likeminded monsters into the fold, making them fierce, frightful, and famous. He built a family.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re not a real family, of course, but who cares? It\u2019s the face that matters, and that\u2019s what the public sees. Hollywood has the Coppolas, Z movies have the Von Schrecks. They may not look alike, but when you\u2019re dealing with a Scream Queen, you know you\u2019re getting commitment to the art of the scare. To quality. And what a commitment! For 70 years they\u2019ve expanded their hold over the genre to television, novels, stageplays, and even video games. They have controlling shares in multiple streaming services, and traveling horror revues based on classics like <i>Curse of Stabula, The Killings on Amberly Lane, </i>and <i>Mutant Holocaust High School!</i><br /> <br /> There\u2019s a reason for all this mythmaking, of course, one that goes beyond dedication to the craft. Ask any Nosferatu and they\u2019ll tell you a simple truth: Fear tastes better. Above all, the Von Schrecks are performative predators. They seethe a sensuality that\u2019s both alluring and repulsive, and not just from the director\u2019s chair. See the editor, sitting in the cramped room, splicing frame by frame of his victim\u2019s final moments; see the starlet stalking the set, hair smeared with thick red streaks her fans think is stage blood; see the producer, a spider keeping the wheels ever turning with money, favors, and Vitae.<br /> <br /> Cults and fan clubs are the bloodline\u2019s stock and trade, and many Scream Queens use these networks to recruit blood dolls, ghouls, and agents (or the rare triple threat). That said, a vampire can only wait so long before people start asking questions about their unaging visage on celluloid. Each Scream Queen has only a short time in the limelight before a \u201ctragic demise,\u201d followed by a decades-long refractory period before they can reemerge as a spiritual and physical successor. Those decades of downtime give them plenty of time to come up with some really wicked ideas.<br /> <br /> Von Schrecks walk the razor thin edge between exposure and overexposure. They write, shoot, and star in despicable acts of depravity, selling their \u201cart\u201d to an audience as bloodthirsty as any vampire. As the Family\u2019s influence grows, their ability to market their crimes spreads. When enough horror stories oversaturate the market, it\u2019ll be impossible to tell the difference between fantasy and reality.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> Do you want influence, money, and power? Fuck no! You want the <i>screams</i>. You crave them! It doesn\u2019t matter if they come from blood spattered teens at a lakeside cabin or brainless fans at a low rent sci-fi con. Being a Von Schreck is being immortal in a way even the eldest vampire couldn\u2019t understand. It\u2019s to be remembered, feared, and loved for being a monster \u2014 forever. You really can have it all.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> Because you love it. That tingle at the bottom of your spine, that tension in your shoulders telling you to run, that quickened step up the basement stairs. That\u2019s us, baby. We\u2019ve sown the seeds of fear on silver screens and late-night airwaves for generations. We\u2019ve rewritten humanity\u2019s subconscious fears to be both insidiously specific yet deliciously addictive. Fear us. Feed us. Worship us. Got it? Great. Now\u2026 roll camera!<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> Everyone wants to be a star, but there\u2019s only enough room for one leading lady. Only one of us can be the brightest, and we can never really be happy for our siblings. Sure, we\u2019re not actually a family, but that doesn\u2019t mean we can\u2019t be just as dysfunctional \u2014 and lethal \u2014 as the real deal. And then there\u2019s the problem with visibility. Sometimes our love of the spotlight goes a bit\u2026 overboard. But who hasn\u2019t dealt with bad press? Or a few stalkers.<br /> <br /> <b>Rumors (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cThere\u2019s a new trend going around Christian streaming services \u2014 Jesus horror, if you can believe it. They\u2019re like normal horror movies, but filled with all sorts of evangelical stuff from Revelation and the apocrypha. And the worst part? They\u2019re getting popular. The people watching them might not even realize they\u2019re supposed to be, yanno, scary. They\u2019re converting people.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Religious film has always evoked a powerful response from the faithful and their wallets. For 14 years, the second highest grossing R-rated movie of all time was The Passion of the Christ, and smaller streaming platforms can afford to target specific social groups, like evangelical Christians. A married pair of Sanctified Von Schrecks, Paulette and Jackson, realized leaning into the bloodier, seedier parts of the Bible could tap into a market that would normally shun anything that even hints of horror. The couple are making hand over fist on this venture, doing the Dark Prophet\u2019s work on a national scale. Their next flick, <i>The Life and Death of Saint Longinus</i>, is going to be huge. Be not afraid? Fuck that.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-15T12:15:46-08:00","id":1432330,"title":"","content":"I love the Von Schrecks; they're this perfect blend of cheesy and genuine, because they really, sincerely love their work. They're <i>proud </i>horror movie monsters, thank you.<br /> <br /> I really want to see a genuinely good Christian Horror Flick. I'm also pretty sure that actually penetrating the heads of people who genuinely believe in The Moral Alternatives is a quixotic task, because actual talent in a scary movie would require an amount of empathy and gore that it wouldn't be presentable, and worse, might interest the flock in things not their leaders. But doing one good enough to the point where real evangelicals regard it as a threat to their authority would be spectacular. Saint Longinius as the anti-hero would be spectacular, as it leans into how utterly destructive and inhuman Rome could be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-15T12:31:26-08:00","id":1432331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1432330#post1432330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the Von Schrecks; they're this perfect blend of cheesy and genuine, because they really, sincerely love their work. They're <i>proud </i>horror movie monsters, thank you.<br /> <br /> I really want to see a genuinely good Christian Horror Flick. I'm also pretty sure that actually penetrating the heads of people who genuinely believe in The Moral Alternatives is a quixotic task, because actual talent in a scary movie would require an amount of empathy and gore that it wouldn't be presentable, and worse, might interest the flock in things not their leaders. But doing one good enough to the point where real evangelicals regard it as a threat to their authority would be spectacular. Saint Longinius as the anti-hero would be spectacular, as it leans into how utterly destructive and inhuman Rome could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're a super fun concept, and I think the author walked the line between campy and genuinely terrifying really well. They probably have my favourite bloodline origin in the book (&quot;Once upon a <s>midnight darkly</s> time in Hollywood...&quot;)<br /> <br /> To pull back the curtain a tad, the Von Schrecks are the ones who changed the most of the new bloodlines over the course of development. The basic idea was there from the start, but they weren't initially a fake (found?) family, and their powers were more about doing horror film tropes with Nightmare than the haunted movie powers they have in the final version. The horror trope thing was a cool idea, but basic Nightmare covers a <i>lot </i>of that if you just present it the right way narratively, though some of their Devotions were tweaked and ended up in chapter three as more generic Nosferatu powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-15T12:44:25-08:00","id":1432333,"title":"","content":"Also, because I don't get to show these off as much as I'd like, our logo artist did a fantastic job on the Von Schreck symbol:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/RPYkNTR/Von-Schreck.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-16T13:13:29-08:00","id":1432430,"title":"","content":"Happy Saturday! Have a preview!<br /> <br /> The Keepers of the Dark are the third of our four new bloodlines. The Keepers ward the world against chthonic gods (or so they say), and wage an eternal cold war with the Lygos over control of the depths.<br /> <br /> The Keepers and the Lygos were developed in tandem by their mutual authors. Both writers had similar ideas about Nosferatu and primordial gods, and they decided it would be more interesting to present two sides of the coin on that concept.<br /> <br /> <b>Keepers of the Dark<br /> <br /> &quot;You shouldn't have come down here. I hope you're comfortable, you'll be staying awhile.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Have you ever made a mistake you wish you could take back? One that seemed like nothing at the time, but then spiraled out of control and changed your life forever? What would you give to take it back? What would you give to keep the past buried forever? Some secrets are worth killing over. Or worse. The Keepers of the Dark understand that better than anyone.<br /> <br /> Humankind is blissfully unaware of the hungry beasts squirming beneath their feet. The dark corners of the earth shelter terrors that cavort upon the planet\u2019s mantle. They are hungry, they are angry, and they are desperate for a way out. Unlucky for us, these writhing aberrations have help. Cultists and other fanatics build elaborate lies to venerate them as gods, and some are even foolish enough to think their worship will elevate them above the chattel in the end to come. The Keepers have sworn their Requiems to delay this end. It\u2019s their duty, after all, as they\u2019re the ones who started us down this doomed path.<br /> <br /> Eons ago, a brood of Nosferatu dug greedily and deeply in service to a lust forgotten to history. Gold? Secrets? Power? Only one thing is certain: what they were searching for was less important than what they found. These beings, which the Keepers call Chthons, were nightmares without form, older than time and hungry as the void. In their hubris, these Haunts did the unthinkable: they woke them up.<br /> <br /> Those who survived became the Keepers of the Dark. A secret society bound together by cursed blood, they work without rest to keep the things beyond at bay. These self-appointed Wardens track cults, arcane artifacts, and other Chthonic influences around the globe, and each brings their own special talents to the fight against the darkness. One is a globetrotting archeologist who delves into tombs, stealing relics, weapons, and histories that could reveal critical weaknesses in the Chthons. Another is a librarian of a boundless archive, risking her mind to take statements from traumatized mortals and supernatural creatures who\u2019ve survived the Chthons. Yet another was once a simple miner who now constructs mazes under the largest cities of the world, working to trap the enemy beneath the earth forever.<br /> <br /> Indeed, perhaps the greatest asset the Keepers possess is their ability to forge powerful domains called Labyrinths. Within these twisting mazes, the Keepers seek to slow the rise of the Chthons and trap their minions in an endless black spiral. Don\u2019t mistake them for heroes, however \u2014 their utilitarian philosophy overwhelms any semblance of morality they may have once had. The Keepers are the ultimate pragmatists, and will partner with everything from Belial\u2019s Brood to the Seers of the Throne if it gives them an edge. The Wardens don\u2019t care about the nature of their allies, or the cost such allegiances may extract from their souls. No cost is too high to pay to stave off the coming dark.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> You\u2019ve felt it. You\u2019ve seen it. You think this world is broken, cracked like a rotten egg with the foul stench of corruption oozing out. The truth is worse: The world isn\u2019t broken, but it <i>will </i>be. Our tainted reality is but the first issuance from things that pupate in the deep, dark below. You cannot stop them. But we can.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> What would you do to save your family? Your lover? Your home? Your neighbor? Now round up. What would you do to save them all? The long and wretched dark is drawing near, and we will do anything to stop the clock from striking midnight. If the price is our souls, so be it, but we will drag you to hell along with us if it furthers even an inch of our cause.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> Nietzsche got at least one thing right \u2014 the dark stares back, and it\u2019s enough to break the most jaded soul. It takes a pure, raw dedication to keep the dark at bay, and even the slightest crack lets it in. It rots us. Changes us. It hollows us out and turns us into something awful. No one tells us this before we accept the duty, and once you fall, you don\u2019t come back.<br /> <br /> <b>Story Seed: Chthonic Taxonomy</b><br /> <br /> So, what are the Chthons really? That depends on the story you want to tell:<br /> <br /> <b>The Chthons are vampires.</b> Perhaps they\u2019re childer of the first Nosferatu, or the Brothers Worm of legend. They could also be what happens when a Strix possesses a vampire so long the fusion warps their shared physical frame, or antediluvian elders in the end stages of the Noctuku Strain. Maybe they\u2019re not so easily defined, representing a form of ur-vampire that existed long before the Kindred became Kindred.<br /> <br /> <b>The Chthons are unrelated to vampires. </b>The Chthons are the Insatiable of <b>Beast: The Primordial</b>\u2026 or the Idigam from <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b>\u2026 or the True Fae from <b>Changeling: The Lost</b>. Maybe they\u2019re a melding of these creatures, some horrible accident of fate that seeks to mend itself with the purifying blood of humanity.<br /> <br /> <b>The Chthons are Infrastructure. </b>These beings aren\u2019t really \u201cbeings\u201d at all, but dormant mechanisms of the God-Machine. Awakening these structures hinders/helps the God-Machine by disrupting/reactivating a forgotten system, which may attract the attention of angels, or the Unchained.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T12:03:04-08:00","id":1432527,"title":"","content":"And now, our final bloodline preview!<br /> <br /> The Candymen are probably the bloodline that changed the least in second drafts and development. Their bane was the only really big alteration: originally they could only feed from characters with low Integrity, or those who had experienced a recent breaking point. That wasn't a bad concept, but it required the ST to keep track of NPC traits that almost never matter, and because Integrity isn't tied to ethics, it didn't really fit with the bloodline's amoral outlook. Their final bane resembles the Ventrue weakness from <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b>, but with more of an emphasis on the victim's physical characteristics.<br /> <br /> <b>Candymen</b><br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Hello, young folks! Care for a free sample? That's right, the first taste is always free!&quot;</b><br /> <br /> It starts with a craving. A gnawing at the base of your sternum coupled with a tickle in the base of your skull. A buzzing fly of a thought: Just one more time. Just one more taste. The urge grows, skips like a broken record, and soon your entire being is a painful repetition of the longing you told yourself you wouldn\u2019t give into again. Why did you have to take that first taste?<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t your fault. Not really. The Candymen knew just what you wanted. They always know, because they mix it with love.<br /> <br /> The Candymen are peddlers of sweets and narcotics who probe that weak spot in the human psyche keyed to want and need. They\u2019re genial, kind, and garish, if a bit weird, and ever so generous. The first taste is always free, and no matter how much adults warn kids about that phrase, it doesn\u2019t stop people from taking a bite. Doesn\u2019t stop them from getting hooked, either. Later, they\u2019ll tell themselves they should\u2019ve known from his smile, so wide it almost split the skin. They should have known from her laugh, shrill and tinged with the punchline of a joke they didn\u2019t know they were part of \u2014 yet.<br /> <br /> The Pushers run vast networks of dealers and salesmen, ready to sell their mothers\u2019 teeth for another hit. Why take a domain by force when you can win with kindness? When the Candymen roll into a territory, their first step is to find whoever moves drugs or sweets and offer to improve their recipes, from independent chocolatiers to street corner meth dealers. Soon, every supplier in town is moving wares sweetened by the Candymen, and that\u2019s when the real fun begins.<br /> <br /> A Candymen\u2019s greatest pride comes from her creations. From Vitae infused confections to moonshine brewed in a bloodstained bathtub, these vampires consider themselves artistes. Among their ranks you\u2019ll find everything from amateur bakers to master chefs, and university chemists to biker crank cooks. Can you hear it? The rusted ice cream truck doesn\u2019t make a noise as it rolls down the suburban street, silent as the grave until the music pipes out of its speakers and lures children of all ages to buy a frosty treat. Can you smell it? The skinhead with the blood smeared smock smashes up crystals reeking of cat piss and acetone, and yet you can\u2019t stop salivating. Can you taste it? The European confection shop has sat on the corner for as long as you can remember, but how they stay in business is anyone\u2019s guess. Your friends dared you to go inside, and its elderly owners offered you a free sample you couldn\u2019t refuse. Now you belong to the shop.<br /> <br /> For the Candymen, there\u2019s nothing more satisfying than watching a customer take that first hit, reach the highest high, and then come crashing down. Nothing is more fulfilling than the trembling hands of a hungry junky. It takes careful craftsmanship to get the best flavor out of a human soul. It\u2019s all about the taste, after all.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> You want to be wanted. Who doesn\u2019t? And the best part about being wanted is that, once you are, no one cares what you look like, dress like, or act like. Not as long as you make them feel good. And the thing is, you actually want to do better! You want to make people happier than happy. You want to make them feel pleasure at a level above ecstasy. You want to gatekeep the taste of magic and wonder like a faucet of pure, unsaturated joy. You want to be everything they need, and the cause of anything they\u2019d do for another taste of bliss. Who wouldn\u2019t?<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> We\u2019re monsters, it\u2019s true. We\u2019re fair though, and always upfront about the cost. The first taste really is on the house, and we\u2019ll offer with a smile and no strings. But make no mistake: the next will cost you so much more than cash. It\u2019ll bleed you dry one bite at a time, until we discard you like a candy wrapper. Fear us because your life is just a fun-sized treat.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> Maybe taste isn\u2019t everything. Ultimately, we\u2019re chasing the same high as everyone else, except we keep eroding our clients looking for our own perfect flavor. What we really want is what we can never have: purity. No matter how hard we try, how much we refine or formulas, everything is tainted. All of it.<br /> <br /> <b>New Devotion: Sugar Rush </b><b>(Vigor \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> There\u2019s nothing like the high that comes from a taste of a Candyman\u2019s supply. Pushers often use this Devotion to recruit athletes and soldiers to their ranks, or to bolster their retainers.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 2 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>2 Vitae<br /> <br /> <b>Requirement: </b>The vampire uses her bloodline gift and spends additional Vitae, included in the cost.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>None<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> <br /> For the rest of the scene, all who eat the vampire\u2019s product gain her Vigor dots as a bonus to Physical actions, pushing their bodies to the human limit. However, every exceptional success on these rolls self-inflicts a point of lethal damage. At the end of the scene, subjects suffer the Lethargic Condition until they get a full night\u2019s rest, or another hit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-18T11:51:14-08:00","id":1432621,"title":"","content":"Happy Monday! Time for another preview/excerpt.<br /> <br /> Since we've run out of bloodlines, let's do some ghoul families. Along with an update of the Gravenors from <b>Ghouls</b>, the Kobayashi are one of two new families in <b>Better Feared</b>. They have a really fun concept that invites both espionage thrillers and family dramas, and they're designed so you can plug them into the Tokyo setting from the core (though they would work in any venue).<br /> <br /> <b>Kobayashi: The Ones Who Take Your Place</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I can be whoever you need me to be.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> \u201cKobayashi\u201d is one of the most common surnames in Japan, so tracing a history of this ghoul family is difficult. Their crest appears in historical documents concerning the hiring of ninja, but not the black-clad acrobats of Hollywood movies. Real ninja (more often called shinobi) were masters of disguise, taking on the appearance of servants, laborers, and peasants in order to get close to their targets. The family that became the Kobayashi were adept at this sort of infiltration, and would replace even members of a victim\u2019s inner circle to fulfill their contracts. It\u2019s said the look of horror that befell a victim\u2019s face \u2014 as a stranger they thought a trusted friend plunged a knife into their hearts \u2014 was an unspeakable horror.<br /> <br /> The first recorded instances of the name Kobayashi being associated with Kindred comes during the Meiji period. Family legend has it that an assassin infiltrated the household of a noble by the name of Fujita, who was suspected of foul deeds following a withdrawal from the public eye. The agent impersonated one of the lord\u2019s retainers, but when he pushed a blade between the nobleman\u2019s ribs, Fujita merely looked on in confusion, before beating the would-be killer nearly to death. Fujita, a Nosferatu, spared the assassin\u2019s life because of how impressed he was that a mere human could fool him so utterly, and for the potential he saw in such a skillset. He bound the Kobayashi agent with his blood, and bid him to return with the rest of his family.<br /> <br /> After this meeting, human records note Fujita\u2019s numerous public daylight appearances. Keeping both his huma influences from waning, as well as infuriating his Kindred rivals, Fujita became an influential figure in his clan, one of the few Japanese Haunts to still enjoy his prestige after the Embrace. Thanks, in no small part, to the Kobayashi. In later years, he began to allow other Nosferatu to make use of his family for a price, but jealously guarded them from the influence of other Kindred.<br /> <br /> Fujita eventually fell into torpor, and thereafter falls out of the historical record. The Kobayashi\u2019s assets were acquired by the Hototogisu Group (<b>Vampire</b>, p. 266) before any Kindred-led zaibatsu could take control them. At first, the Nosferatu were angered by this new development, but, to their surprise, the Hototogisu allowed the Kobayashi to continue offering their services, more-or-less as they always had, the only difference being where the Haunts pay their fees and favors.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> In modern nights, business is booming. Throughout Japan, and Tokyo especially, \u201crental culture\u201d is rampant, and companies will rent out dates, siblings, friends, or even parents. If these services exist, then it\u2019s just a small hop to hiring a better version of yourself. Is it immoral to hire a professional liar to manipulate the emotions of your former loved ones? No more than hiring someone to pretend to find you hot. Incorporated under the Hototogisu in the mid-90s in order to formalize their business model, the Kobayashi are now as much a company as they are a family. The advent of cellphones and the Internet has lessened the need for face-to-face interaction, but Japan has a strong cultural drive to take care of important matters in person. This can make things awkward if you have a face full of eel\u2019s teeth, or your stare makes people feel like boils are bursting across their skin.<br /> <br /> The Kobayashi serve Japan\u2019s Nosferatu by becoming them, or at least becoming how they used to be. Need to negotiate an important financial deal, but the other party won\u2019t meet outside banking hours? Can\u2019t bear the thought of your family thinking you\u2019ve died, but somehow still need to join them at the shrine on New Year\u2019s Day? Did you get a little sloppy feeding one night, and now need to put on some public daytime appearances so that reporter will get off your back? These are all problems the Kobayashi can solve.<br /> <br /> The family trains its members in the arts of disguise and mimicry, using special plastic surgery for exacting or long-term clients. Prospective doubles work directly with the Nosferatu they\u2019re impersonating in order to ensure the disguise is as perfect as can be. They also spend a significant amount of time stalking anyone they\u2019re expecting to interact with frequently in order to learn habits and routines, and avoid any game-breaking slip-ups. In exchange for these exclusive services, Mimics take Nosferatu Vitae as part of their payment, and the family enjoys the favor of the clan in general. Sometimes they work for other clans, but the Nosferatu are the most in need of their skills. The Kobayashi work hard to make their clients feel as though they\u2019re doing their friends and family a great service, and not at all like they\u2019re paying a stranger to live among them like a human cuckoo bird.<br /> <br /> For now, the Mimics are restricted to Japan and Southeast Asia, but the family heads are beginning to consider untapped markets in both Europe and the Americas.<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes:</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b> Daeva: </b>They would never want our services, even if they needed them.<br /> \u2022 <b> Gangrel: </b>How <i>does </i>one wear sheep\u2019s clothing?<br /> \u2022 <b> Mekhet: </b>Not even they remember who they used to be.<br /> \u2022 <b>Nosferatu:</b> Our most generous patrons, and our most demanding clients.<br /> \u2022 <b> Ventrue: </b>Acting like you\u2019re in charge isn\u2019t the same as actually being in charge. Trust me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 02-07-2021, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T04:54:07-08:00","id":1432674,"title":"","content":"So, I find it interesting that there seem to be hints of a connection between Better Feard's Yagnatia and the Licinii of Requiem for Rome. They seem to have the Julii Bane presented in a Thousand Years of Night, there's a hinted connection to Rome and one of their nicknames is the 'Pretenders', like the Licinii. It feeds my inner conspiracy theorist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T05:34:13-08:00","id":1432677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1432674#post1432674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I find it interesting that there seem to be hints of a connection between Better Feard's Yagnatia and the Licinii of Requiem for Rome. They seem to have the Julii Bane presented in a Thousand Years of Night, there's a hinted connection to Rome and one of their nicknames is the 'Pretenders', like the Licinii. It feeds my inner conspiracy theorist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't noticed that- it actually makes way too much sense. Also, their Discipline spread is less &quot;Nosferatu with Dominate&quot; and more &quot;Julii with Nightmare&quot;. That, together with their Bane and their second Bloodline Origin and the Roman origin rumor (and maybe the thing about the werewolf connection), directly leads towards them being related to the Julii in some way. Also, just to spice this theory up, the Betrayed (which hate the Yagnatia), may also be related to the Julii (iirc, the escaped vampire came from Rome), so yeah it looks very plausible that the Yagnatia have some Julii blood in their bloodline. I would probably play it that like in the Twists of Blood section, there are two branches of the Bloodline- one from before the Julii escaped to their land which have the original Bane, and one after the Julii entered the Bloodline, which carries the newcomer's Bane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T11:48:29-08:00","id":1432696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1432674#post1432674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I find it interesting that there seem to be hints of a connection between Better Feard's Yagnatia and the Licinii of Requiem for Rome. They seem to have the Julii Bane presented in a Thousand Years of Night, there's a hinted connection to Rome and one of their nicknames is the 'Pretenders', like the Licinii. It feeds my inner conspiracy theorist.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not paranoia if they\u2019re really out to get you... &gt;_&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T13:01:48-08:00","id":1432705,"title":"","content":"Happy...Tuesday! Yeah! Let's have another ghoul preview.<br /> <br /> The Gravenors first appeared in first edition's <b>Ghouls</b>. <b>Ghouls </b>is a book I have a bit of a love/hate relationship with: It's got a lot of great material, but it's also pretty puerile at times. It's from 2005, and it <i>exudes </i>early installment weirdness. That said, the Gravenors as-presented in <b>Ghouls </b>aren't too different from the ones in <b>Better Feared</b>, but I've shifted their creepiness from &quot;isolated inbred hicks&quot; (and all the baggage that came with that) to &quot;doomsayer occult detectives&quot;, which I feel opens them up a lot more for stories. Enjoy!<br /> <br /> <b>Gravenor: The Ones Who Watch and Wait</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cShh! They\u2019re listening.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> The night the vampire crawled up the steps of the Gravenor Estate was the last its halls knew happiness. This is almost a family motto, but it\u2019s never a lament. It\u2019s a reminder that a veil has lifted, and it can never fall again.<br /> <br /> Late in the 19th century, the Gravenors were hog farmers. Still are, in fact, and wherever the family digs in, its slaughterhouses are sure to leave a few stains. Meat on the table was of great concern to Roderick Gravenor, the family\u2019s patriarch and self-made moral guide. It was on his mind when he crossed the Atlantic from Wales, searching for a buck in the cash-rich USA, and it remained so as he built a small empire in flesh. That\u2019s what made his family rich, but tonight its all that keeps them out of poverty. Now they have more important beasts to worry about than pigs.<br /> <br /> The creature at the door was half-starving. He\u2019d smelled blood off the farm\u2019s abattoir from miles away, and followed the scent to the family\u2019s manor. Unconcerned with the Masquerade, he begged to feed on the hogs, and in exchange, promised to reward the kindness. In taking up his offer, the Gravenors likely didn\u2019t know the devil\u2019s bargain they\u2019d made, though some wonder if their knack for reading occult tea leaves proceeded this meeting, and inadvertently guided the decision.<br /> <br /> Grigor Swancott was an outcast, even for a Haunt. A talented occultist, he was once a respected member of the All Night Society, known for his deep breadth of arcane knowledge. Even the Shadows envied his visions, but Grigor fled his Requiem when he uncovered a secret. Over the course of many nights, he told the Gravenors of the things coming for his clan. Some say he carried on into daylight hours, forcing the family to board up the windows of their estate (boards that have never come down). In his studies and dreams alike, he\u2019d discovered creatures from the depths of a forgotten realm, who would soon rise to reclaim the Nosferatu to the soil and worms \u2014 and then all Kindred. The Gravenors call them coblynau, a name taken from Roderick\u2019s memories of the mines in Wales.<br /> <br /> When he was finished, the Gravenors were transformed, their nightmares now in sync with their accidental master. Some say they became ghouls without ever tasting his blood, tainted by the force of his horror.<br /> <br /> Was it really his fear that changed them? Perhaps, but truth is often better served with terror, and this was no simple application of Nightmare. No one knows if Swancott chose the family for a reason, or if he really did just stumble upon them. Some say he recognized the Gravenor name from the old country, but if so, he's never admitted it. The better question is, was he right?<br /> <br /> The jury\u2019s still out.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> Soon after he bore his soul (and blood bonded the entire family), Swancott fell into torpor, and apart from flashes of lucidity and garbled prophecy, he hasn\u2019t returned. Kept in a secure tomb/shrine on the estate, countless mundane and occult protections keep all but the family\u2019s elders and most trusted servants out of his resting place. The Gravenors dedicate their lives to protecting their torpid master, and preparing for whatever\u2019s coming for him. They even still feed his corpse, taking what they need of his Vitae to retain their own immortality.<br /> <br /> Globalization and industrialization has put the family business on a slow decline, but they still grasp at a shadow of their old empire. The little capital they make from hogs goes into building their properties up into fortresses, assuring that, when the coblynau do rise, the family isn\u2019t caught unawares. Part of each day is dedicated to watching for signs, prognosticating their own awful fate and that of their master.<br /> <br /> This obsession has left the family eccentric and insular, even for Nosferatu ghouls, but it\u2019s also provided them a niche in the All Night Society. The Watchers are occult consultants, supplementing the meat business by hiring themselves out to the covenants as supernatural detectives and problem solvers. Their inherent talent for spotting the strange rivals even that of the Shadows\u2019, and they\u2019ll serve any master with need of such lore. Most Gravenor ghouls are bound to Swancott, but a few branches of the family have arrangements with other Nosferatu. While they don\u2019t enjoy as much autonomy, they\u2019re also less wrapped up in their family\u2019s apocalyptic beliefs.<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes:</b><br /> \u2022 <b>Daeva:</b> At least they admit the gaps in their knowledge.<br /> \u2022 <b>Gangrel: </b>Anything that claims it can\u2019t be killed is, without exception, eminently killable.<br /> \u2022 <b> Mekhet: </b><i>What do they know?</i><br /> \u2022 <b>Nosferatu:</b> Canaries.<br /> \u2022 <b>Ventrue:</b> If only they could see what was coming for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T15:26:16-08:00","id":1432727,"title":"","content":"Oh, and here's something I put together for fun while I was doing layout: A bloodline playlist! It's in book order, so you don't have to guess which is which:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/playlist/0dCt3BhzvgByQXaiCXV7kt?si=PJHADVbgQjmIBZswCfEEgA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/playlist/0dCt3BhzvgByQXaiCXV7kt?si=PJHADVbgQjmIBZswCfEEgA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/playlist/0dCt3BhzvgByQXaiCXV7kt?si=PJHADVbgQjmIBZswCfEEgA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://open.spotify.com/playlist/0dCt3BhzvgByQXaiCXV7kt?si=PJHADVbgQjmIBZswCfEEgA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T11:50:10-08:00","id":1432811,"title":"","content":"Time for a preview!<br /> <br /> Here's our last ghoul family: The Cham\u00e9nos. Another new one to the setting, the Unwanted straddle a strange line between social and genetic ghoul family (see <b>Half-Damned</b>). They appear spontaneously in Nosferatu subcultures around the world, all with the same weakness and strength...<br /> <br /> <b>Cham\u00e9nos: The Ones Who Were Thrown Away</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Save your pity. I have purpose; you have nothing.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> In every culture across the globe, children are precious gifts, shining lights representing the future of their communities\u2026 except the ones who aren\u2019t. Sparta cast out \u201cimperfect\u201d infants to die, and the Incans sacrificed their most beautiful children to ensure the favor of the gods. In the filthy streets of Industrial London, the desperate tossed wailing babes into the Thames rather than suffer more mouths to feed. Even today, unwanted newborns can be found on church steps, at hospital backdoors, or cast aside in dumpsters.<br /> <br /> However, what\u2019s thrown away can be found again. It\u2019s unclear when Nosferatu began collecting discarded children, or even where the practice first originated. Was it in the holy caves of the Andes Mountains, waiting for the sun-priests to leave so they could steal away their tributes? Or perhaps it started with watching churchyards in medieval France, snatching bassinets before the priests knew they had a new arrival.<br /> Regardless of methods, the why of it remains constant. What better way to secure retainers than from those humans other mortals cast out? No one goes looking for a divine sacrifice; no one files a missing person report for a baby a trash can.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu rear these Unwanted as blood-slaves to their rescuers, indoctrinated into rejecting human society in favor of the All Night Society. At certain times and places in history, discarded children have been so common that the Haunts have created whole secret Foundling communities, living out of sight of the rest of civilization and with one generation training the next. As the world grew smaller, however, Haunts realized what they thought of as a local practice is in fact mirrored all around the globe. Now they\u2019ve started to talk to each other.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> While dozens of regional terms for the Unwanted exist, \u201cCham\u00e9nos\u201d has the widest recognition, and some even adopt it as a surname. This name was coined by a family of ghouls in Greece who claim descent from Sparta\u2019s rejected infants, and they\u2019ve made the greatest strides in connecting the various tribes of Foundlings in the modern world. Not so much a single family as an eclectic network of communities, Cham\u00e9nos around the world are remarkably similar, no matter their cultural origin. Rather than everyday people forced into bondage, as many ghouls are, the Unwanted are raised with the idea that serving a Nosferatu master is the highest possible calling, and look forward to the day they become half-damned. The rest of the All Night Society might view that as brainwashing, but the Cham\u00e9nos see it as duty. After all, without the Haunts, their ancestors would have died fresh from the womb \u2014 something their masters are quick to remind them of.<br /> <br /> This abnormal dedication is what the Foundlings are best known for, and they serve their patrons with a remarkable zeal, even for ghouls. Their extreme devotion can be a mixed blessing, however. All ghouls become obsessed with their domitors eventually, but a Cham\u00e9nos\u2019 life revolves around his master in a way even the rankest Vitae addict would find a tad overwrought.<br /> <br /> Rarely able to hold down normal jobs, groups of Foundlings often turn to crime to meet their masters\u2019 needs, as well as their own. Drug cartels and black markets are common, with the Unwanted using the profits on behalf of their family, and a few of their would-be clients as dinner for their patrons.<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes:</b><br /> \u2022 <b>Daeva:</b> Their \u201cdevotion\u201d is a fleeting imitation of the real thing.<br /> \u2022 <b> Gangrel: </b>They act like being alone is good.<br /> \u2022 <b>Mekhet: </b>Always sneaking in where they aren\u2019t wanted.<br /> \u2022 <b>Nosferatu: </b>Our saviors and our charges.<br /> \u2022 <b>Ventrue:</b> They make the best faces when you tell them to fuck themselves.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Now that we've reached the end of the ghoul families, what kind of preview would you all like to see next? I'm not going to be too many more after this, but I have a few options: Would you like to see one of the Horrors, or one of the sample Necropoli?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T13:19:49-08:00","id":1432947,"title":"","content":"I'm personally more interested in seeing the horrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12220-dark-lord-potato","name":"Dark Lord Potato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T14:11:02-08:00","id":1432957,"title":"","content":"Pssssssssssttttt...<br /> <br /> Show them a necropolis...<br /> <br /> I'm not biased at all... XD XD XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T14:31:54-08:00","id":1432958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Lord Potato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1432947#post1432947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm personally more interested in seeing the horrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm never one to fly in the face of popular opinion.<br /> <br /> The Noctuku as a concept go all the way back to <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b>. In <b>VTM</b>, they were the Nictuku, proto-Nosferatu who hunted their clanmates on behalf of their antediluvian master. In <b>Requiem</b>, they became a bloodline of Nosferatu cannibals, forced to exist on the outskirts of the All Night Society.<br /> <br /> Our take on the Noctuku had a lot of ink spilled over them. I noted above that we were originally just going to continue with the bloodline interpretation, albeit a corrupted one with some special mechanics. However, that interpretation just didn't work for me once the first draft came in. It felt arbitrary to separate them into the Horrors chapter if they were still just a bloodline with a fourth Discipline and a bane, and much too player-facing for something that (mostly) is going to be used as an antagonist. However, the author \u2014 right at the last minute, where all great ideas form \u2014 included an optional sidebar about them being a viral infection. <i>That </i>was much more interesting to me, and it brought the whole idea together. Obviously there are some parallels with Malkavia here (though you'll have to wait until <b>[REDACTED]: Ventrue </b>to find out how we deal with that), but unlike the M, the Noctuku Strain is something you can actually put under a microscope. It's a true virus, but it just happens to only affect Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> In terms of systems, a suite of inherent abilities made more sense than dots on a character sheet. As for customizations, Phagia began as Protean Devotions, but again, it felt too player-facing. To unpack that term a bit, I mean things that you can spend XPs on for your character, and that are built with an eye toward player utility. Instead, I wanted something that didn't cost a single XP, and was brutally unfair. So, we repurposed the systems from those Devotions, and turned Phagia into a series of Dread Powers. They're not really the same as the ones in the Blue Book, since many of those are redundant for Disciplines, but the format worked well. I considered just removing their access to Disciplines altogether, but that felt <i>too </i>far off the baseline. Though, if you were using them for a mortals game, that might work as a stand in for having to track full-on vampire powers..<br /> <br /> Anyway, I've gabbed on enough. Meet the Noctuku:<br /> <br /> <b>The Noctuku Strain: The Ravenous Dead</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cGo? I\u2019ll let you go. But run hard. I want to work up an appetite.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The Nosferatu are stronger, sneakier, and more terrifying than other vampires. They are nightmares of the dead, and draw strength in their own horror. Yet predators rarely exist in a vacuum. There\u2019s always a bigger fish, and even monsters have boogeymen.<br /> <br /> The Noctuku are what keep the Nosferatu awake in the day. The only thing more terrifying than their grotesque powers is their hunger for the flesh of other Kindred. That, and that any Nosferatu could be one \u2014 or become one.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> The Noctuku Strain has plagued the Kindred for thousands of years. Defiant and Sanctified researchers have found the earliest records of the contagion in records dating back to pre-contact North America, ancient Greece, and even the steppes of Mongolia. These geographically distinct locations offer eerily similar accounts: A vampire, easily identified as a Nosferatu, arrives in the community, and soon after all the other Nosferatu start to behave strangely.<br /> <br /> Where the accounts differ is the cause. Ojibwe Kindred believed Noctuku had been punished for devouring their own kin, while the Mongolians thought the Nosferatu\u2019s innate filth made them hosts for unclean spirits. The Greeks saw the Noctuku as a cult of the Titan Cronus, who devoured his own children to maintain his throne. Whatever the fine details, one thing is consistent \u2014 when Noctuku arrive, Kindred vanish.<br /> <br /> The Strain is particularly virulent in periods of famine and war among mortals. Time and time again, such events have primed Kindred for small explosions of new Noctuku. When food becomes scarce and violence reigns, vampires have little choice but to turn on each other for sustenance, but by then it\u2019s too late to ever go back. One bite is all it takes.<br /> <br /> <b>A Plague of Hunger</b><br /> <br /> The Strain is a malignant virus transmitted through the blood and flesh of infected Nosferatu. Presently, only the Haunts are vulnerable to this virus, but some Kindred scientists fear the day the Strain mutates. Once it fully gestates, the infection is incurable. All it takes is a drop of Vitae or a tainted bite to become infected, and then it\u2019s only a matter of time. The strong-willed can stave it off, but those who give in to the virus\u2019s new desires change rapidly. The Haunt\u2019s body begins an agonizing metamorphosis that makes them stronger, faster, and deadlier. The virus twists and reshapes their mouths to be better at ripping and tearing, and instills a deep and consuming hunger for dripping raw meat, still warm off the bone.<br /> <br /> Even more horrific are the changes to the Noctuku\u2019s mind. The Beast never rests for most vampires, but a Noctuku\u2019s Beast becomes an equal partner, constantly urging wanton violence and bloodlust. The Noctuku are always hungry, always hunting, and the only way to truly satisfy their need is the flesh of their former Kindred.<br /> <br /> <b>The Cannibal Kings</b><br /> <br /> Despite their ravenous appetites, the Noctuku aren\u2019t feral. Indeed, once the infection completes its transformation, they appear no stranger than most other Nosferatu, and that\u2019s how they hide. The Noctuku blend in like any vampire among the kine, albeit with a more restrictive diet. To keep up the charade, Cannibals must remain ever mindful of the local Kindred ecology, and rely on separation and discretion when hunting.<br /> <br /> Their specialized feeding requirements mean the most successful Noctuku tend to fall into two categories: nomads, or apex predators in metropolises where Kindred often come and go. The Cannibals are highly territorial for this reason \u2014 which is one of their few positive traits, as it means they almost never come in groups. Almost.<br /> <br /> However, one is often more than enough. The Noctuku are stronger, faster, and deadlier than other Kindred. Their ferocity and scarcity are such that they\u2019re relegated to myth outside the Necropoli, who pass whispered stories of solitary Cannibals devouring entire broods. If the Nosferatu are talking about the Noctuku, it\u2019s already too late.<br /> <br /> <b>Noctuku Strain (Persistent)</b><br /> <br /> You are infected with the Noctuku Strain but are not yet one of the Cannibals. As the disease takes hold, you lose the 10-again quality on all actions any night you resist the urge to consume Kindred Vitae or flesh. This hunger is so great that the mere presence of other, uninfected Kindred provokes hunger frenzy, though it only applies once a scene. If presented with Kindred Vitae, you suffer a \u20134 modifier to resist frenzy as if you were starving. However, you can spend a point of Willpower to ignore this hunger for one scene. Ending this Condition requires you not to feed on anything stronger than human blood for one night per dot of the infecting Noctuku\u2019s Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> Should you consume Vitae, you regain a spent Willpower in addition to the usual effects of drinking vampire blood. If you indulge in flesh, you regain all spent Willpower. Each time you give in, the time it takes for this Condition to run its course resets. If you indulge in Kindred Vitae or flesh a number of times equal to (11 \u2013 the infecting Noctuku\u2019s Blood Potency), the infection enters its active stage: Resolve this Condition and gain the traits of a Noctuku.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> A Noctuku\u2019s blood or bite, rampant diablerie.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Accept your place among the Cannibals.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat:</b> Infect another vampire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 01-21-2021, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T14:34:19-08:00","id":1432959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1432957#post1432957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pssssssssssttttt...<br /> <br /> Show them a necropolis...<br /> <br /> I'm not biased at all... XD XD XD</div> </div> </div> </div>TOO LATE.<br /> <br /> (I'll do a Necropolis tomorrow. Let's make it author's choice: The Coal Shafts, The Lost Necropolis, Popobawa's Roost, or the Rusted Graveyard? I GUESS we could do Mike's too, but who cares about that guy???)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Pl