uiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T21:31:47-08:00","id":1433013,"title":"","content":"I'm just wondering, what was the main theme yall went for when designing the bloodlines and ghoul families? I'm sorry if that question is one yall would rather not answer (which i completely understand)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T01:43:22-08:00","id":1433026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1433013#post1433013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just wondering, what was the main theme yall went for when designing the bloodlines and ghoul families? I'm sorry if that question is one yall would rather not answer (which i completely understand)</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally happy to answer questions!<br /> <br /> Theme-wise, my major note to the bloodline writers was to emphasize the horror. Some of the early drafts (and this included my own) were a tad too generic; they were good bloodlines, but not necessarily great <i>Nosferatu </i>bloodlines. The Gethsemeni, for instance, had a lot more emphasis on breaching the Masquerade in their first draft, whereas the final version focuses on the holy horror of being a prophet touched by the indefinable hand of God. All the bloodlines evince a different kind of scary: the unknown, knowing too much, being a cog in a machine, addiction and decadence, and so on.<br /> <br /> The ghoul families are more about the ways Nosferatu blood (for lack of a better term) fucks you up. Haunts have the most overt curse of the Damned, and that twisting nature can extend to their servants. Nosferatu ghouls are just <i>weirder </i>than those of other clans, and all of our ghoul families are a little off-kilter. For example, while we never come right out and say it, the Chamenos are really a subtype of ghoul rather than a family. We used the ghoul family mechanics for convenience, but they're more akin to things like mnemonic ghouls and Heisenbergs (both from <b>Half-Damned</b>). I've always liked the idea that Nosferatu ghouls mutate a bit, which is something you can find in <b>Masquerade </b>a bit more than <b>Requiem</b>, so that was the guiding light there.<br /> <br /> From a broader perspective, the overarching theme of the book was &quot;Lonely Together&quot;, and everything in <b>Better Feared </b>ties back to that. Nosferatu and their ghouls are insular rejects, so they had better get used to each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T11:52:44-08:00","id":1433080,"title":"","content":"A fine Friday to you all!<br /> <br /> The following is one of our five sample Necropoli. While about half the Warrens chapter is taken up with background and systems, the rest is dedicated to these example domains. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> did 4/5 of them, and he did a fantastic job as usual. The following is from Lethbridge, Alberta, in a continuing effort by he and I to Canadianize the Chronicles of Darkness as much as possible, eh?<br /> <br /> <b>The Coal Shafts: Sik-ooh-kotok (Lethbridge), Canada</b><br /> <br /> Deep in the Albertan south, Sik-ooh-kotok has always been a bastion for the Nosferatu. The Coal Shafts started as a hiding place from the hated sun, but now they drip with power as the greatest Kindred come home to roost. Intrigue and danger are afoot, though, as the other clans test their chains, and covenants threaten to tear the domain apart from within.<br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> The first of us arrived in the 1870s and 80s when the settlers found coal along the Old Man River, but most of us didn\u2019t arrive until the first railways came in \u201985. We snuck into the mines, picking off our victims one by one. Who would question a miner feeling exhausted and sick after a long shift? And if someone disappeared in the darkness, well, it\u2019s a dangerous job\u2026<br /> <br /> The mines started closing in the early 20th century with the oil boom in Western Canada. Coal wasn\u2019t profitable anymore, not worth descending down the shafts where sharp teeth waited to prick the skin. It was a mixed blessing for us. The Warren was now truly ours, a safe place where Haunts can rest away from mortal eyes, but our food no longer wandered close to our homes.<br /> <br /> As Lethbridge adapted to a new global economy, we ventured out of our mines and seized control of the town that was rightfully ours.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> The first Kindred in Lethbridge were Haunts, and it remains Haunt territory tonight. That much didn\u2019t change, but our purpose evolved. As the University became more and more central to the city\u2019s lifeblood, we fused our faith with scientific innovation. The Lancea et Sanctum and Ordo Dracul joined forces to understand the Kindred condition and build the best monster possible. The Warren\u2019s dark caverns, far from where any mortal can hear the screams, echo with their gurgling experiments, creating monsters that are both holy and blasphemous.<br /> <br /> Their alliance also keeps the other covenants in check, although such vulgar politics aren\u2019t supposed to matter in the Necropolis. The Sanctified have the sheer numbers to sway the domain, but the Dragons are hot on their heels, and aren\u2019t above bribing the Judges with new monstrosities to get their way. It\u2019s a dangerous night when a priest returns to the surface with a grin on his face, covered in soot and blood. And that\u2019s ignoring the Establishment\u2019s debauched parties and the Firebrands\u2019 hidden dynamite caches, secreted away amongst the twisting tunnels. The mines aren\u2019t just a place to hide from the sun \u2014 they let us hide from each other, plotting and conniving our way to rise to the All Night Society\u2019s pinnacle.<br /> <br /> These politics are the biggest threat to our society. All are equal within the Coal Shafts, but the covenants still jockey for power and influence, even if they go out of their way to make it look like they aren\u2019t. Make no mistake though \u2014 the other clans would love to take the foundation we\u2019ve built and reel all the benefits for themselves, without having to do the hard labor. It\u2019s all a twisted rosebush labyrinth: beautiful to look at, but twisted and dangerous to touch. Rest assured, your nights in Lethbridge won\u2019t be quiet, but they sure as hell won\u2019t be boring.<br /> <br /> <b>Secrets and Lies (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> Sik-ohh-kotok\u2019s Nosferatu still age, albeit slowly. Punch an elder hard enough and you\u2019ll find he doesn\u2019t have bone under his dead muscles anymore, but coal. Given enough time, this anthracite petrification oozes its way into the vampire\u2019s flesh, stiffening and immobilizing the ancient creature. Before that happens, the elders roost deep within a secret chamber in the Necropolis, becoming twisted, bloody stalagmites in their clan\u2019s lair. Drinking the blood dripping from these humanoid coal formations allows younger Haunts to tap into the elder\u2019s knowledge and power until the next sunrise.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems</b><ul><li><b>Heart: </b>The elevator shafts of the abandoned coal mines.</li> <li><b>Focus: </b>Uncover secrets about the Kindred condition (Information, formerly Protection). Residents of the Necropolis gain a Beat whenever they contribute to the study of vampires, or invent a unique power of the blood, like a Devotion.</li> <li><b>Benefit: </b>When spending Willpower on Academics, Occult, or Politics rolls about vampires, residents gain the 8-again quality.</li> <li><b>Burden:</b> Let no member of another clan enter the mines.</li> <li><b>Clot:</b> Guardian Swarm (undead rattlesnakes)</li> <li>Residents of the Coal Shafts have access to the <b>Bleak Annals </b>and <b>Dark Hub </b>Merits.</li> </ul><br /> -----<br /> <br /> What does all that system stuff do? Well, this is just an excerpt, I'm afraid...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T12:51:29-08:00","id":1433087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1433026#post1433026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Totally happy to answer questions!<br /> <br /> Theme-wise, my major note to the bloodline writers was to emphasize the horror. Some of the early drafts (and this included my own) were a tad too generic; they were good bloodlines, but not necessarily great <i>Nosferatu </i>bloodlines. The Gethsemeni, for instance, had a lot more emphasis on breaching the Masquerade in their first draft, whereas the final version focuses on the holy horror of being a prophet touched by the indefinable hand of God. All the bloodlines evince a different kind of scary: the unknown, knowing too much, being a cog in a machine, addiction and decadence, and so on.<br /> <br /> The ghoul families are more about the ways Nosferatu blood (for lack of a better term) fucks you up. Haunts have the most overt curse of the Damned, and that twisting nature can extend to their servants. Nosferatu ghouls are just <i>weirder </i>than those of other clans, and all of our ghoul families are a little off-kilter. For example, while we never come right out and say it, the Chamenos are really a subtype of ghoul rather than a family. We used the ghoul family mechanics for convenience, but they're more akin to things like mnemonic ghouls and Heisenbergs (both from <b>Half-Damned</b>). I've always liked the idea that Nosferatu ghouls mutate a bit, which is something you can find in <b>Masquerade </b>a bit more than <b>Requiem</b>, so that was the guiding light there.<br /> <br /> From a broader perspective, the overarching theme of the book was &amp;quot;Lonely Together&amp;quot;, and everything in <b>Better Feared </b>ties back to that. Nosferatu and their ghouls are insular rejects, so they had better get used to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I am especially happy to hear about your thoughts on nosferatu effect twisting even ghouls (from your writeup of the chamenos, it definitely sounded less like a family and more of a twisted type of ghoul, which made it sound absolutely awesome) <br /> <br /> I'll be getting the book this weekend!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-23T12:53:57-08:00","id":1433175,"title":"","content":"Let's have another Night Horror preview!<br /> <br /> The Nowhere Men are entirely new to <b>Vampire</b>, not being based on any first edition material. I'll let the write up below explain their niche, but first I wanted to talk a little about why I like them so much. The Nowhere Men don't have mechanics. They don't have traits or Dread Powers; they just work when you (the Storyteller) need them to. Okay, they have <i>one </i>mechanic, which is the Condition they place to track their victims, but even that's mostly a narrative tool. The Nowhere Men aren't meant to be something STs use to vex their players: they're a tool you can use to weird up your games, and get players to think creatively about how they use their powers, and how they solve their problems when they can't just hide in the shadows.<br /> <br /> <b>Nowhere Men: Stalkers of Shades</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cHow can you not see them?! They\u2019re right there! They\u2019re right there! They\u2019re right\u2014\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Every culture has urban legends. These stories reinforce morality through fear, instilling cultural taboos and promoting group conformity. The hook-handed killer on Lover\u2019s Lane may or may not have existed, but his legacy puts a damper on teenage sexcapades. Bloody Mary won\u2019t really get you if you say her name three times in a mirror, but it\u2019s a bonding ritual. None of these things are real. They can\u2019t hurt you.<br /> <br /> Until they do.<br /> <br /> Even the All Night Society has urban legends, and the Nowhere Men are a favorite of the Nosferatu and Mekhet. These men \u2014 or what are assumed to be men \u2014 are invisible stalkers, wraiths who hunt vampires that spend too much time hiding away from mortals. Use your Obfuscate too often, they say, and the Nowhere Men will take you, piece by piece. It\u2019s a warning against becoming too reliant on one\u2019s Disciplines. They\u2019re just a fairy tale. They can\u2019t hurt you.<br /> <br /> Until they do.<br /> <br /> The Nowhere Men aren\u2019t just a story. They exist in a place beyond human perception, or even supernatural perception. Impossibly, they can only be seen by vampires using the powers of Obfuscate, who are also the only ones who can be their victims.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> Nowhere Men appear as humanoid voids in the fabric of reality. Their features force the eye to slide to the margins of their forms, and it\u2019s difficult to focus on them for long. Any vampire who uses Obfuscate gains their notice.<br /> <br /> If a Nowhere Man can reach a victim and touch \u2014 just touch \u2014 a piece of her, he\u2019ll take it. A hand vanishes. An eye disappears. A leg slips off into nothingness. In each case, nothing remains except a raw, red wound, one that looks as if it\u2019s pressed against clear glass. The Nowhere Men are never sated for long, however, and they\u2019ll keep hounding their prey until, piece by piece, they take every part. Pity the powerful, for if the Nowhere Men catch one of them demonstrating full mastery of the shadows, they may not bother taking parts.<br /> <br /> Kindred snatched up by the Nowhere Men cease to be. They cannot be traced with any known technology, Discipline, or blood magic. They vanish from the world, leaving behind little more than a memory as they\u2019re stolen away to somewhere \u2014 nowhere \u2014 else.<br /> <br /> <b>Close Encounters</b><br /> <br /> Modern vampires teach their childer that Obfuscate tricks the mind, but maybe the truth is more subtle. Some ancients believed it drew upon a darkness at the edge of awareness, or even on the veil between worlds. Whether or not they were right, one thing is certain: Obfuscate attracts the Nowhere Men, and it\u2019s the only way the creatures can interact with physical beings. They may be denizens of some world in-between, or perhaps they just hunt it, and live in another shadow reality.<br /> <br /> Why they hunt is a mystery, and those who\u2019ve survived encounters offer a myriad of theories: They are broken ghosts or spirits, prohibited from interacting with the rest of their kind; they are the souls of the damned, trapped between worlds; they are elder vampires, so heavy with blood their very existence clouds the minds of their prey.<br /> <br /> While any vampire can be a victim of the Nowhere Men, it\u2019s the Haunts and Shadows who\u2019ve encountered them most. However, adding yet more grist to the rumor mill, it seems they have a preference for Nosferatu victims, when given a choice. One Dragon scholar speculates they were once a Haunt bloodline, one that drifted too far into the dark, and now seeks to return to the flesh world by juryrigging new physical forms. An Acolyte mythologist says he has evidence the Brothers Worm sealed these creatures in an annex in the depths of the Underworld, and the Nowhere Men avenge themselves on their childer.<br /> <br /> Or maybe? They just like the taste of Haunt.<br /> <br /> <b>Rumors (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cThe urban legend about the Nowhere Men is exactly that. Want to know what\u2019s powerful enough to see through invisibility and overpower vampires? What else? Vampires. Duh.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Just before World War I, Kindred archeologists recovered an centuries-old scroll from a crypt beneath Kyoto. Among other things, it contained a short poem called \u201cThe Man Shaped Like Nothing,\u201d which described a creature who transformed first into a bloodthirsty oni, and then into a being of pure nothingness. Recently, scholars from the Lancea et Sanctum have begun to re-examine poems like this, as well as similar stories in ghost and demon mythology. They\u2019ve found a disturbing prevalence for words like \u201cvoid\u201d or \u201cabsence,\u201d frequently mistranslated as synonyms for shadow, darkness, and night. If this correlates to a real phenomenon, not only is it possible the Nowhere Men were once Kindred, but it may be there are many more of them, and yet more to come.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T12:26:09-08:00","id":1433420,"title":"","content":"Good Monday to you all! I took a break from excerpts yesterday, but I've got a fresh one for you now.<br /> <br /> The Fear Eaters are the kind of antagonist I love to find in a Night Horrors book. They're a simple design and a strong concept, and you can use them easily as either villains or allies. They'd also work well in other games, like <b>Hunter</b>, or even <b>Changeling</b>. They have lots of potential story hooks, too, and I think the author hit all the right notes to make them creepy, scary, and a little sympathetic.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the structure of the Fear Eating Merits take a bit of inspiration from <b>Shunned by the Moon</b>, as well as the &quot;minor templates&quot; from <b>Hurt Locker</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Fear Eaters: Taking Your Life Back</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cBreathe in. Deep. Let the fear gather up inside you and then\u2026 swallow it. All of it. See? Better already.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> The Fear Eaters began, as many things do, with trauma. In 1989, brothers Ken and Jason Arden were dared by a group of older boys to break into a neighborhood haunted house in Overland Park, Kansas. It was a sweltering, sticky summer night when the boys went in, and a soupy Midwestern morning when Ken alone escaped, sheet white and nonverbal. He would spend most of his teens in psychiatric wards, suffering the indignities of shock therapy and quack hypnotherapy. Nothing worked. Not until the book arrived.<br /> <br /> If asked, Kenneth \u2014 as he prefers to be called now \u2014 says a distant relative sent him a simple, brown paper\u2013wrapped package on his 16th birthday. In truth, it had no return address. Reading had become Kenneth\u2019s only outlet, so it wasn\u2019t unusual for him to receive books from family and friends. But this one was special. The book was old and charred, with a smiling lithograph on its blackened cover. Neatly printed in gilded letters was the title: On the <i>Consumption of Terror</i>. No author was listed.<br /> <br /> Although half the book was either damaged or missing, he devoted himself to the text. He read it hundreds of times, over and over. Then, one day he asked a shocked orderly if he could call his parents. He checked out of the psychiatric hospital that week and used his family\u2019s guilt to support him as he dedicated the next fifteen years to the study of religion, psychology, and esoterica, all in service to his goal of rebirthing the text of the book. When <i>Fear Eating: How to Take Your Life Back </i>was finally released in 2010, it was an underground hit on the self-help circuit, but the book was only the beginning.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been thirty-one years since the haunted house, and Kenneth has never moved past his terror and grief. It\u2019s helped him realize the book was incomplete for a reason. It needed his fear. It needed his memories of the long-tooth man with the bloodless skin whose smile was torture and whose shrieking laugh had cracked his life open.<br /> <br /> Arden knows others like him are out there, those who\u2019ve also experienced these creatures firsthand. Now he travels the globe searching for them under the guise of an endless book tour. He makes a point to offer one free seminar per city, with a reasonable entry fee for all non-private events. If he takes notice of someone \u201cspecial\u201d at one of these events, they\u2019ll receive an invitation to an exclusive weekend worship. That\u2019s where the chosen learn the true power of Fear Eating.<br /> <br /> <b>The Art of Eating Fear</b><br /> <br /> You can\u2019t learn to eat fear if you haven\u2019t experienced it. Arden and his acolytes can sense those who are open to their teachings, people with the potential to consume fear through exposure. Like, for instance, victims of the Nosferatu. Not all mortals who\u2019ve encountered the Haunts are capable of Fear Eating \u2014 even those who\u2019ve lost blood to them. To become a Fear Eater, one must have lost something in the exchange, more fundamental than just a few pints. Still, the Fear Eaters haven\u2019t been successful just because of vampires. Their seminars can be\u2026 intense.<br /> <br /> Once you\u2019re chosen, the real work begins. Initiates are first taught simple techniques, like meditation, breathing exercises, and mantras to ground them. Then, they\u2019re given an unsafe dose of LSD and walked back through their buried pain, over and over and over until these memories can be summoned as a reflex.<br /> <br /> And it <i>works</i>. Somehow. Calling forth the echo of a past trauma suppresses the fear reflex in the here and now. Fear Eating changes you. It doesn\u2019t make you invincible, but it does make you confident, bold, and decisive. You won\u2019t sweat the small things, like hesitating to ask for a phone number, or failing to speak your mind. The sudden injection of confidence into a life of anxious trepidation leads to sudden and profound changes that, if nothing else, <i>feel </i>like a good thing.<br /> <br /> Once the program takes hold, the book becomes your holy text. You can see the truth Arden hid behind the prose to keep out the unworthy. It\u2019s a simple one: Fear is a lie, and the only way to kill a lie is to make sure everyone knows the truth. You realize the more Fear Eaters you can bring to the cause, the weaker the lie will become, so you start to guide others to seminars, workshops, and events. You give out the book as a birthday present, or the office Secret Santa, or leave strategically tabbed and dogeared copies on public transit.<br /> <br /> <b>It\u2019s Not a Cult</b><br /> <br /> Of course not. It\u2019s a mindset \u2014 a way of life. There\u2019s no grand network of Fear Eaters holding each other accountable, or love bombing each other into complacency. Perish the thought. Sure, you meet a few times a year and chat on forums, but who doesn\u2019t want to be near likeminded people? And yes, maybe they do spend a lot of time talking about the book, re-reading ragged copies, or practicing breathing exercises until they choke. It\u2019s not <i>their </i>fault they\u2019re passionate about something. Isn\u2019t it the same with CrossFit and veganism? You can stop at any time\u2026 but with results like these, why would anyone want to?<br /> <br /> <b>New Merits (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> Through careful training, mind-bending drugs, and regression therapy, adherents of Fear Eating can call on memories of past terror to bolster their spirit. This sudden flash of fear suppresses natural responses to anxiety, be it a stressful situation or the use of a supernatural power. With careful study and cultivation, an individual can radiate fear back at those who would wield it against her.<br /> <br /> To learn these Merits, a character needs to fulfill one of two prerequisites. Either she must have failed a breaking point due to a supernatural power of fear (e.g., Nightmare), or during one of the Fear Eaters\u2019 \u201cseminars\u201d, where they break down their recruits so the healing might begin in earnest.<br /> <br /> <b>Resist Fear (\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Mortal, Empathy \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Fear is fleeting. Your character has learned to wrestle her emotions for control of her mind. She adds her Empathy dots as a bonus to any action to contest or resist social coercion using negative emotion, from mundane intimidation to Nightmare.<br /> <br /> In Social maneuvering, the Fear Eater can spend a Willpower to ignore hard leverage involving intimidation or threats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 01-27-2021, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T18:17:21-08:00","id":1433443,"title":"","content":"Just picked up the book. <i>The Beast That Haunts the Blood</i> gave me actual nightmares back in the day, so I'm looking forward to this. I'm not very far in yet, but when the identity of Charity's stalker was revealed, I audibly gasped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T21:15:17-08:00","id":1433459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1433443#post1433443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just picked up the book. <i>The Beast That Haunts the Blood</i> gave me actual nightmares back in the day, so I'm looking forward to this. I'm not very far in yet, but when the identity of Charity's stalker was revealed, I audibly gasped.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much higher praise than that, quite honestly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T16:54:26-08:00","id":1433556,"title":"","content":"Forgot to post a preview! Oh no! Well, we'll call this an after work one.<br /> <br /> This is another of our sample Necropoli. Unlike the other four, the Quaint Village has an ambiguous location, other than it being in an isolated part of Scotland. We wanted to include at least one you could more easily use as a template, or just plug in to another country altogether.<br /> <br /> <b>The Quaint Village: Scotland, United Kingdom</b><br /> <br /> Have you ever driven through a town that just seems wrong? Where all the people are perfectly friendly, the buildings tidy and well-kept, yet something sets your teeth on edge? Maybe it\u2019s how their smiles all seem a little forced, or how instead of times, all the businesses advertise that they close \u201cat sundown.\u201d<br /> Perhaps you should trust your instincts and not linger too long. Oh, how odd: Your car seems to be out of petrol \u2014 but you could have sworn you had plenty in the tank! No matter, you can get more at the station when it opens tomorrow morning.<br /> <br /> You just need somewhere to stay the night.<br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> To say we\u2019re off the map is putting it kindly. If it weren\u2019t for the Internet, the rest of the country might\u2019ve forgotten we ever existed. Suffice it to say, not a lot comes in, and not a lot comes out. Rarest of all, though, is when something comes back.<br /> <br /> It was only a few decades ago when Dottie Tonner did just that. Most of us were just kids when she left, thinking she was gonna make it big in some city. Instead, she got killed and turned into the monster she is today. Or maybe she was always this toxic, and it just took dying to bring it out in her. Anyway, she was the first vampire the town had ever seen, and we were\u2026 unprepared.<br /> <br /> Dottie doesn\u2019t talk about what happened in the city, like who turned her, or why she came back \u2014 none of that. She sure as hell likes being boss, though. She started small: set up shop in the basement of her own home, turned her parents into blood slaves. Her mom\u2019s still around, but her dad offed himself early. Guess he couldn\u2019t cope with what his \u201clittle girl\u201d became.<br /> <br /> Dottie\u2019s a nasty piece of work, but she\u2019s smart. She took her time, turning or binding anyone in town with authority until we controlled the whole thing, and she controlled all of us. Every Embrace expanded the Warren, and each new victim meant a new basement or service tunnel added to the maze. Whole town\u2019s compromised now, but it still looks normal up above. You need to dig down to find the rot.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> Dottie moved into the courthouse the minute she could get away with it. It had lots of unused basement space (who needs records?) and she needed somewhere to keep the first dissidents. The barely used cellblock was well-built on that front. The court\u2019s a nice, central location, so when she got the tunnels started, we didn\u2019t have to dig far. We\u2019re a small town, and there\u2019s not a single building that doesn\u2019t have some sort of trapdoor, subbasement, or cellar that our underground home links up to.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re always watching, and people who make too much trouble get a new roommate. We feed and terrorize them until they understand it\u2019s better if they just behave. Pretend there\u2019s nothing wrong, just like everyone else.<br /> <br /> Dottie takes on stubborn cases herself, and the lady enjoys her work. Her pet projects are never really the same afterwards, but they never cause trouble again. Between blood and fear, we pretty much have this town sewn up. Oh, the humans realize something\u2019s wrong, no question. Nothing is open after dark, and everyone knows walking outside at night is an invitation to disappear for hours\u2026 or days. They\u2019re not really \u201cmissing,\u201d though. We just take them on a little vacation. We do our best to make sure they survive the experience; scared is good, but we don\u2019t want to push them into desperate \u2014 that\u2019s how you get torch-wielding mobs.<br /> <br /> Visitors are a whole other matter. Dottie\u2019s been a big fish in a small pond for decades now. She gets bored easy, so outsiders tend to catch her interest. Poor sods. Any tourists who stay the night are hers to play with, and presenting her with a catch is the best way to get on her good side. It\u2019s not just us, either. The townsfolk have figured out if visitors stay overnight, things get just a little less awful for them the next couple weeks. They don\u2019t know it\u2019s because the Queen Bitch of this madhouse is busy scaring said visitors to death for her amusement, but they also don\u2019t ask questions when they vanish in the night, either.<br /> People who come through town up above are encouraged to stay, or they might run into \u201ccar trouble,\u201d or even get arrested on some bullshit charge \u2014 anything to keep them overnight. Poor bastards almost never reach wherever it is they were trying to get to, but the rest of us sure appreciate them keeping Dottie busy for a while.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s Dottie\u2019s world, and the rest of us just live in it. Meet her and she seems normal enough, but if she looks at you for too long it feels like a hundred spiders are crawling around inside your skin. Even nastier if she touches you. Worst part? She\u2019s a hugger.<br /> <br /> <b>Secrets and Lies (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> Not all of the population is as under control as Dottie thinks. A group of local teens know how bizarre their town really is, and they\u2019ve been reaching out online to find others with similar experiences. In their desperation, they\u2019re attracting attention from a few groups who would find an isolated town full of vampires very interesting indeed.<br /> <br /> <b>The Quaint Village</b><ul><li><b>Heart:</b> The holding cells beneath the courthouse.</li> <li><b>Focus: </b>Total domination (Control). Residents gain a Beat when they scare a villager into submission, silence someone who\u2019s been asking questions, or otherwise reinforce Dottie\u2019s rule.</li> <li><b>Benefit:</b> Residents take a +5 rather than +3 when spending Willpower on rolls to cow the locals, whether through social or physical means.</li> <li><b>Burden:</b> If able, residents must capture overnight visitors and present them to Dottie, without having tasted their blood.</li> <li><b>Clot: </b>Catacombs</li> <li>Residents of the Quaint Village have access to the <b>Corrupting Influence </b>and <b>Honeycomb Merits</b>.</li> </ul><br /> -----<br /> <br /> We're getting close to the end of material for me to excerpt; would you all like me to finish off the Necropoli, or preview something from the systems chapter?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T21:59:25-08:00","id":1433576,"title":"","content":"You know what I'll say XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=