09-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T10:46:11-08:00","id":1433633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1433629#post1433629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any new books in the making? Like, are you planning on writing about all 5 clans? If yes, is there any particular order you'll follow? (Are the Ventrue close?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep! The Ventrue book is up next! In fact, I\u2019m working on my Malkavia write up today.<br /> <br /> Order is:<br /> <br /> Mekhet<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Ventrue<br /> Daeva<br /> Gangrel<br /> <br /> (We\u2019re working in, uh, looping alphabetical order.)<br /> <br /> After that, we\u2019ll see what the plan is. Maybe a book of lost clans, maybe finally getting around to Bloodlines: The Ageless (that turned out to be a much bigger project than I first conceived.) Or maybe something non-Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T11:59:08-08:00","id":1433640,"title":"","content":"A Wednesday excerpt!<br /> <br /> Not much commentary on this one. This is another of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> wonderful Necropoli, and it offers a wide variety of hooks for <b>Requiem for Rome </b>fans:<br /> <br /> <b>The Lost Necropolis: Tarquinia, Italy</b><br /> <br /> Western Vampires look to Italy as the All Night Society\u2019s birthplace, but Rome\u2019s legacy doesn\u2019t enamor everyone. Some Kindred remember their forebears stalked the night before the Camarilla rose. In Tarquinia, the Haunts work to tear down Rome\u2019s historical fa\u00e7ade, but they may end up going down with it.<br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> Fuck Rome and fuck the Romans. Whether you call our city Tarchuna, Corneto, or Tarquinia, we remember where we came from, and just how much Rome stole from us. European Kindred hate each other, yet half of them are in a mutual circle-jerk over how glorious the Camarilla was, conveniently forgetting the Romans were thieves and killers. Yes, I know we\u2019re all thieves and killers. That\u2019s not the point. We\u2019re honest about what we are, but the Camarilla? They pretended to be more than the monsters, and vampires are still pretending they were better than everyone else.<br /> <br /> The Etruscans, our ancestors, created the first Necropolis, and we Haunts hid in its shadows. I won\u2019t lie and say the times were all good, but our forefathers had something unique that belonged to them, and them alone. Then Rome started growing, leeching culture and lives away from the other Italian tribes. When Etruria finally fell, the Legio Mortuum pillaged our tombs, and the Julii convinced the weakest Haunts to join them and create the fiction of the Roman Necropolis. Those who refused, they staked to the mountainside to greet Apollo.<br /> <br /> I want to be very clear about this next bit: Fuck Mussolini too. That said, when he started renaming places to invoke the Empire, at least he had the decency to pick an Etruscan name. Yeah, the Tarquinii were Roman kings, but they were an Etruscan line. It was about the same time we found the caverns into the old Warren \u2014 the secret library the Julii never purged.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> Tonight, Tarquinia\u2019s Haunts are a Kindred nation apart. Want to know how much restoring our history has changed things? The Invictus and Carthians are working together! Both want to break the Roman stranglehold on our imagination; the Establishment wants Tarquins \u2014 not Romans \u2014 to rule Tarquinia, while the Firebrands insist fixating on an imperial past prevents us from adapting to the present. If our Etruscan legacy can mend that divide, imagine its potential for the rest of the All Nights Society.<br /> <br /> Of course, when I say we\u2019re a nation apart, I mean the Necropolis. We Haunts reclaimed our past, but the others refuse to see the truth, beguiled as they are by the Camarilla\u2019s beautiful lie. We are harsh, and we are ugly, but that\u2019s what it takes to see the truth. So we sit amongst our tomes, working together to devise a better domain, even if it doesn\u2019t reach beyond our Warren. One night, the truth will be free, and when that dusk comes, we\u2019ll be ready. <i>Roma delenda est</i>, assholes.<br /> <br /> <b>Secrets and Lies (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> A ghost claiming to be the shade of Tarquin the Proud, the last king of Rome, guards the Lost Necropolis. The Ordo Dracul are skeptical Tarquin\u2019s shade could have persisted for so long, but the ghost is a useful guardian, so they humor its claims. Unknowingly, the vampires got more than they bargained for, as a masked ghost claiming to be Lucius Junius Brutus hunts Tarquin, hoping to drag him back to Tartarus.<br /> <br /> <b>Residents (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> Leinth, Welcoming Face: Tarquinia\u2019s Acolyte Hierophant is Leinth, who builds her cult to reflect the Etruscan mythology the Romans appropriated and erased. The majority of her Acolytes are Haunts, but she welcomes all clans into the fold, putting her at odds with more conservative Nosferatu, who feel the other clans were complicit in Rome\u2019s crimes. Worse, she allows these non-Nosferatu into her section of the Necropolis, violating its sacred boundary. So far, Leinth and her critics have only exchanged harsh words, but the Necropolis will face civil war if tensions continue to escalate.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lost Necropolis</b><ul><li><b>Heart:</b> Etruscan burial chambers beneath the library.</li> <li><b>Focus: </b>End the myth of the Roman golden age (Sabotage). Residents gain a Beat for vandalizing or destroying Roman artifacts, or engaging in violence over the legacy of the Camarilla.</li> <li><b>Benefit:</b> Residents add +5 rather than +3 when spending Willpower to subvert another vampire\u2019s authority.</li> <li><b>Burden: </b><i>Always </i>challenge myths of past glory and golden ages.</li> <li><b>Clot:</b> Necropolis Specter (\u201cTarquin the Proud\u201d)</li> <li>Residents of the Lost Necropolis have access to the <b>Corrupting Influence </b>and <b>Necropolis Arsenal </b>Merits.</li> </ul><br /> -----<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, let's take a trip to <b>Popobawa's Roost</b> in Dar es Salaam. And on Friday, we'll have one final big excerpt with <b>The Rusted Graveyard</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T13:55:20-08:00","id":1433654,"title":"","content":"One last question (due to some complications, I have not been able to aquire the book yet). Are Necropolises purely a cultural thing among the Nosferatu, or are they mystical in some way (or even just pseudo mystical). If the latter, why the change from cultural to something more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T14:32:13-08:00","id":1433656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1433654#post1433654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One last question (due to some complications, I have not been able to aquire the book yet). Are Necropolises purely a cultural thing among the Nosferatu, or are they mystical in some way (or even just pseudo mystical). If the latter, why the change from cultural to something more?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly cultural, sometimes supernatural. A Warren is usually a social/political affair: it's something the clan got together to form, and the mechanics we provide in the book are just a way of putting numbers on it. For instance, the Quaint Village (above) doesn't have anything occult going on. However, some Necropoli do have supernaturally enforced Benefits and Burdens, or take on strange aspects in the form of Clots, or are built over mysterious places. Vampires in and of themselves are magical beings too, and sometimes the presence of Vitae can corrupt an area.<br /> <br /> That being said, the basic concept of Warrens isn't a supernatural phenomenon like, for example, a mage's Demesne.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T18:09:32-08:00","id":1433669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1433656#post1433656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mostly cultural, sometimes supernatural. A Warren is usually a social/political affair: it's something the clan got together to form, and the mechanics we provide in the book are just a way of putting numbers on it. For instance, the Quaint Village (above) doesn't have anything occult going on. However, some Necropoli do have supernaturally enforced Benefits and Burdens, or take on strange aspects in the form of Clots, or are built over mysterious places. Vampires in and of themselves are magical beings too, and sometimes the presence of Vitae can corrupt an area.<br /> <br /> That being said, the basic concept of Warrens isn't a supernatural phenomenon like, for example, a mage's Demesne.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh ok, thank you! I'm sorry for the hold up, but I promise I will get the book, I love your (and @Second Chances) work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T21:08:59-08:00","id":1433678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1433633#post1433633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After that, we\u2019ll see what the plan is. <b>Maybe a book of lost clans</b>, maybe finally getting around to Bloodlines: The Ageless (that turned out to be a much bigger project than I first conceived.) Or maybe something non-Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it's going to be a long while before you get the clanbooks done, and I don't want to stop you if you'd rather do something else at that point, but I want it to be noted that I'd kill for a lost clans book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12220-dark-lord-potato","name":"Dark Lord Potato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T22:00:42-08:00","id":1433680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Lord Potato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1433678#post1433678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it's going to be a long while before you get the clanbooks done, and I don't want to stop you if you'd rather do something else at that point, but I want it to be noted that I'd kill for a lost clans book.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, just a little preview of my thinking on that, it would probably be similar to our clan book updates, but with bloodlines from a bunch of the canonical lost clans. Then we'd have a few optional lost clans, new to the book. But that's a ways off...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 01-28-2021, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T12:05:16-08:00","id":1433730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1433175#post1433175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Nowhere Men: Stalkers of Shades</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Having finally picked up the book, these things were definitely my favorite bit. I was also pleasantly surprised by the updated system for the flaw mechanics in <b>Beast that Haunts the Blood</b>, especially the advice given on how to broaden it so that the other Clans can play, too. Good stuff.<br /> <br /> And of course, the updated the Necropolis rules are very cool. Time to write new versions of the Necropolis Merits for my Caporetti and Telamones conversions...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T12:55:30-08:00","id":1433737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1433730#post1433730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having finally picked up the book, these things were definitely my favorite bit. I was also pleasantly surprised by the updated system for the flaw mechanics in <b>Beast that Haunts the Blood</b>, especially the advice given on how to broaden it so that the other Clans can play, too. Good stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I <i>loved </i>the flaw mechanics in the old book, and doing an update of them was in my outline before I even decided which bloodlines we were doing. The old system is actually pretty solid but, for obvious reasons, in <b>VTR2E </b>it makes a lot more sense to anchor it to Humanity rather than Blood Potency. Humanity is already connected to banes, and moves up and down a lot more than BP. That's a very &quot;me&quot; design choice: I like systems that are accessible to neonate characters. Like, you can't realistically see the height of the old system unless you're playing a game that goes over a looooooong period of time, and even with the new Experiences system, it's still a tall order. The only other really big change in the conversion was no longer applying it to Attributes. I felt it was simultaneously a bit too powerful and a bit too debilitating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And of course, the updated the Necropolis rules are very cool. Time to write new versions of the Necropolis Merits for my Caporetti and Telamones conversions... </div> </div> </div>In my pre-planning for this book, I <i>almost </i>included the Telamones as one of the updated bloodlines, but I ultimately decided they were too close to the Lygos. The Shades needed the update more, in my estimation.<br /> <br /> Exclusive Necropolis Merits would be a great bloodline gift for the Telamones! Maybe they can create Clots?<br /> <br /> Anyhow, let's get to the excerpt.<br /> <br /> Yesterday, I promised to take you on a tour of Popobawa's Roost. Bar none, the Roost the weirdest of the five sample Necropoli. In my outline, I asked for &quot;Something strange and unexpected,&quot; and boy did <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> deliver on that...<br /> <br /> <b>Popobawa\u2019s Roost: Dar es Salaam, Tanzania</b><br /> <br /> Dar es Salaam is a city on the go, one of the hubs anchoring the Swahili coast. As mortals rise, so do the Haunts. They hide among the kine masquerading as the popobawa, a local cryptid, and have made a good Requiem out of the deceit. They aren\u2019t the only ones, though. As blood slips over grinding gears, the God-Machine\u2019s angels watch the Haunts mutate into something darker and hungrier than before.<br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> Vampires have hunted the Swahili Coast ever since the first trade boats sailed south along the Indian Ocean. We\u2019ve been here as long as anyone could remember, but our Warren in Dar es Salaam is new. Dar started off small. The socialist government\u2019s Ujamaa policies discouraged urban growth, so the kine stayed in the countryside \u2014 something about cities being hotbeds of parasites and capitalist oppressors. That changed in the 80s when Dar\u2019s population went from a couple hundred thousand to a couple <i>million</i>. We saw the apartment buildings rising into the night sky and seized one for our own. We hollowed it out, turning it into our personal stronghold, a place where Haunts could feast in the burgeoning cityscape.<br /> <br /> In the 90s, mass hysteria gripped the city. An evil spirit known as the popobawa roamed the streets, inciting mass panic in the population. No Kindred has ever reliably reported its existence, but we saw another opportunity and seized it. We weren\u2019t behind the sightings, but come on \u2014 a bat-like creature causing fear? That sounds like a Haunt to me, and we are opportunists to the core. We became mapopobawa stalking the night, using the legend to our advantage and giving the Roost its name.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> Apparently, we the only mapopobawa in Dar\u2019s shadows. It started when a bunch of neonates swore they spotted humanoid bats flying around one night, monsters made of gears and bleeding oil. Weird enough shit that we thought they might have caught a touch of the old hysteria themselves. Then our elders started seeing them too.<br /> <br /> At first, we feared the Owls, returned from the pages of Islamic legend once again, but these were something different. Most stalk mortals, driving them mad with fear, but sometimes they appeared to our fellow Kindred, demanding they leave the area. Most of the time they just watched us from afar. It\u2019s unsettling, knowing something is out there with plans for you and yours. Not that we would know anything about that.<br /> <br /> Then the mutations started. Maybe we\u2019d watched these technological mapopobawa for too long, but whatever the cause, the blood clotted in our veins, metastasizing into cancerous gears beneath our skin. Haunts started <i>becoming </i>the legend we pretended at, growing leathery wings and bizarre growths that stopped us from blending in with the kine. As far as we know, only our Warren is subject to these mutations \u2014 if any other Kindred are cursed with them, they hide it well. We need answers; otherwise the Roost really will be home to mapopobawa.<br /> <br /> <b>Residents (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Niku, Masquerade Breech:</b> Niku thinks Kindred society is bullshit, particularly when it comes to the Masquerade. The other clans, the other covenants, they beat the Haunts down just like the colonizers and slavers did all along the Swahili Coast for centuries. He knows other Carthians have good intentions, but they get so caught up in politics and theory that they miss the bigger picture. This is Africa\u2019s century, the time when the booming metropolises will replace helpless villages within the global consciousness. Dar can be on the forefront of the Movement, but it will take the cooperation of Kindred and kine to reach its full potential. Disregarding the Masquerade, Niku\u2019s reached out to shamans and occultists, fostering mortal allies around the Necropolis so that when the revolution begins, the other clans will find themselves outnumbered. If you need to find a psychic or medium, Niku is your bloodsucker, but he needs help staying one step ahead of the Kindred who disapprove of his methods. It\u2019s getting harder to keep things quiet with each passing night, as his allies grow hungrier for the Roost\u2019s secrets.<br /> <br /> <b>Popobawa's Roost</b><ul><li><b>Heart: </b>The basement of the Roost.</li> <li><b>Focus:</b> Provide a safe space for the growing Nosferatu population (Protection). Residents gain a Beat when they defend another Haunt socially or physically, contribute to fortifications in the Roost, or (more recently) fend off attacks from \u201creal\u201d mapopobawa.</li> <li><b>Benefit:</b> On rolls drawing on the Popobawa\u2019s legend, residents gain the 8-again quality on Intimidation and Nightmare powers. The latter includes Devotions.</li> <li><b>Burden: </b>Use the myth of the popobawa when hunting at least once in a lunar month.</li> <li><b>Clot:</b> Uncanny Altar (a piece of Infrastructure disconnected from the God-Machine)</li> <li>Residents of Popobawa\u2019s Roost have access to the <b>Home Turf </b>and <b>Necropolis Arsenal </b>Merits.</li> </ul><br /> -----<br /> <br /> Tomorrow shall be our final excerpt when we check in on The Rusted Graveyard in Nouadhibou, Mauritania. However, I enjoyed waxing on about the flaws system, so would anyone find it interesting if I did a few development posts? Just reasons why we did one thing or didn't do another, and how things evolved over time. I've been kind of doing that all along, but I'm sure I could come up with more. The Necropolis system had a fair amount of development between drafts, for instance, and I had some specific goals in mind when I decided to base it on lodges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T14:25:33-08:00","id":1433745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1433737#post1433737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my pre-planning for this book, I <i>almost </i>included the Telamones as one of the updated bloodlines, but I ultimately decided they were too close to the Lygos. The Shades needed the update more, in my estimation.<br /> <br /> Exclusive Necropolis Merits would be a great bloodline gift for the Telamones! Maybe they can create Clots?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, I like the sound of that! Like some sort of unholy geometry stuff, like what the Keepers of the Dark have going on, but a lot less focused on keeping things in. I was originally thinking something more like, &quot;they do the existing Necropolis stuff, but better,&quot; and I will still post that, but this is a lot more interesting...<br /> <br /> But yeah, the Lygos definitely needed an update far more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tomorrow shall be our final excerpt when we check in on The Rusted Graveyard in Nouadhibou, Mauritania. However, I enjoyed waxing on about the flaws system, so would anyone find it interesting if I did a few development posts? Just reasons why we did one thing or didn't do another, and how things evolved over time. I've been kind of doing that all along, but I'm sure I could come up with more. The Necropolis system had a fair amount of development between drafts, for instance, and I had some specific goals in mind when I decided to base it on lodges. </div> </div> </div>I think the development talk is fascinating, personally! I like seeing how and why people make the design decisions they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T12:46:41-08:00","id":1433825,"title":"","content":"Final excerpt, and something to enjoy for the weekend! On Monday I'll be back with a few development notes, if I can come up with anything interesting to say about them.<br /> <br /> <b>The Rusted Graveyard: Nouadhibou, Mauritania</b><br /> <br /> Stereotypical Nosferatu inhabit graveyards, but nothing says it has to be human ones. Nouadhibou hosts the world\u2019s largest ship graveyard, sitting forlornly in the city\u2019s bay, making it the perfect forum for an aquatic Necropolis. These marine Haunts hunt for blood amid the dilapidated hulls, but new horrors rise from the deep and threaten to consume the entire Warren.<br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> The Sahara is a bitch to deal with at the best of times, and that\u2019s before the Embrace, so there\u2019ve never been many vampires in Nouadhibou. Still aren\u2019t, but our population boomed back in the 80s when a bunch of fishing companies went belly up and scuttled their ships in the bay. It\u2019s an eyesore for mortals, but for us, it\u2019s refuge from the oppressive, omnipresent, bastard ball of fire in the sky that\u2019s just waiting to smite us. A place to sleep where the mortals won\u2019t bother us is worth the indignity of traipsing through rusty water every time we want to feed.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> Nouadhibou\u2019s got the dubious honor of having the largest ship graveyard in the world. Funny, right? We sleep in both a junkyard and a graveyard. The Necropolis is growing now that we have space to expand into, but it\u2019s pretty much the extent of the entire domain. We sleep in the sand and the mud, safely buried underwater; not like we need to breathe any more. The sun can\u2019t touch us as blood mingles with salt water, and we cultivate bloody corals in aquatic Wyrm\u2019s Nests. We might be waterlogged corpses, but we\u2019re <i>predatory </i>waterlogged corpses, as silent and deadly as the sharks and angler fish the Blood twists us into.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s easier to count the Kindred who aren\u2019t Haunts, so we graciously let them into the Necropolis, as long as they don\u2019t start shit. These nights, we need all the help we can get. A few years back, we noticed some mortals behaving strangely before some damn ocean bugs tore their way out of their mouths. We killed the little shits, but the Dragons among us were still able to identify them \u2014 some freaky shit they called <i>Cymothoa sanguinaria</i>.<br /> <br /> Point is, they\u2019re some sort of underwater, vampiric parasite. We didn\u2019t find many at first, but now the seafloor is crawling with the little shits, and some of them aren\u2019t so little any more. Whatever\u2019s going on, these bugs are mutating, growing larger, and hungering for Vitae.<br /> <br /> <b>Secrets and Lies (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> The Dragons don\u2019t know where the C. sanguinaria infestation is coming from, but they desperately want to find out. Rumors of the bizarre parasites draw researchers from across North Africa and Southern Europe to Nouadhibou, and not all of them are willing to announce their presence, or play nice with the Graveyard. In secret bunkers, foreign Dragons implant the parasite into humans and ghouls alike, not caring if they destabilize or destroy the Necropolis in the process.<br /> <br /> <b>The Rusted Graveyard</b><ul><li><b>Heart: </b>A large fishing trawler at the center of the Graveyard.</li> <li><b>Focus: </b>A private place away from the sun and the kine (Protection). Residents gain a Beat when they bring new Haunts into the Necropolis, or keep interlopers away.</li> <li><b>Benefit:</b> Necropolis members can move underwater unimpeded by tides or currents. They do not suffer penalties to Physical rolls for being underwater.</li> <li><b>Burden: </b>Patrol the ocean waters at least once per week.</li> <li><b>Clot:</b> Guardian Swarm (twisted sea life). This doesn\u2019t include <i>C. sanguinaria</i>; they\u2019re much worse than a Clot.</li> <li>Residents of the Rusted Graveyard have access to the <b>Home Turf </b>and <b>Lost &amp; Found </b>Merits.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T12:12:31-08:00","id":1434632,"title":"","content":"Hey all!<br /> <br /> So, I know I said I'd provide some development notes, but my mind kind of blanked when I sat down to write them (Malkavia has been taking up a lot of brain space...). Plus I think I've said pretty much all the really interesting things \u2014 at least the ones that interest me. If any of <i>you </i>have questions, though, feel free to toss them up on this thread.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's a little bonus excerpt, because why not? The only commentary I have on this is that those names for non-Nosferatu &quot;necropoli&quot; where in my original outline, and might have been one of the first things I came up with when I was drafting the shape of the book.<br /> <br /> <b>Necropoli</b><br /> <br /> The Haunts exist on the margins of the All Night Society, shoved into the deepest shadows and the narrowest cracks. The rest of the Damned don\u2019t think about Nosferatu unless they have to; out of sight is out of mind. While the clan may gripe about that treatment, in truth, this indifference suits them well. If the other clans found out what they were building down in the depths, they might try to take it for their own. Or destroy it.<br /> <br /> Necropoli are places only the Nosferatu rule. Whether underground networks of tunnels and tombs, miniature empires hidden in hollowed out warehouses, or whole towns ripped away from the map, these domains are unique among the clans. One Necropolis is a series of decommissioned and forgotten subway tracks, restored and oiled with blood, allowing swift travel beneath the city streets. Another is an old mine just outside of town, where troupes of men shuffle off to trade their blood for the treasures revenant miners pry from the earth. A third is the twisted wreck of an enormous tanker ship, half-sunk into the silt of the bay, where dead things watch the glimmering surface above for their next meal. Necropoli are fortresses and open forums, record halls and larders. Their forms and functions are as twisted and varied as the Haunts themselves, and every bit as disturbing to outsiders. They\u2019re where the Haunts can truly be themselves.<br /> <br /> Only the Haunts gather together in such communities, and have done so for millennia. The Nosferatu have always been builders \u2014 they had to be. Serpents and Lords can force themselves into the halls of power and have mortals dancing to their tune in a night; Shadows slip between the camera feed frames to inhabit forgotten spaces, with other residents never the wiser; and Savages don\u2019t need a roof as long as they have a patch of dirt. But Haunts aren\u2019t gladhanders or sneaks or survivalists. They\u2019re <i>monsters</i>, and monsters live in the muck, under bridges, caves, and sewage drains, away from the terrible truth of light.<br /> <br /> Necessity is a good teacher, and the Nosferatu are excellent students. A few pieces of sheet metal here, a trapdoor there, and what began as a shelter from the sun and society becomes a home. Still, a home isn\u2019t home without neighbors\u2026 but who wants to live with a monster? The other monsters, of course, and fuck all the ones who pretend to be something else.<br /> <br /> Other clans aren\u2019t welcome down in the depths. Their authority is worth less than the runoff dripping down the rusted pipes. Rejects rule the Warrens, and any \u201cKindred\u201d foolish enough to forget aren\u2019t going to survive the visit.<br /> <br /> <b>Ex Urbe Mortis</b><br /> <br /> The first Necropolis worthy of the name was built beneath Rome, ironically at the behest of another clan. The Dead Julii desired a place of magnificence from which to rule the Camarilla, and they bade the Worms of Rome to burrow deep, and craft a dark reflection of the city above. The Roman Necropolis was a thing of white marble and proud columns, the first and last city created by the dead, for the dead.<br /> <br /> When Rome burned above, the Necropolis remained below, and parts of it still stand tonight as the last shards of the Camarilla, a legacy of its lowest members. The Haunts have never forgotten this, and while other Kindred do their best to rise to greater heights, the Nosferatu dig ever deeper, even as the surface falls to ash.<br /> <br /> <b>In the Covenants</b><br /> <br /> In order to sustain their numbers, most Necropoli are inter-covenant affairs. However, a given city might have enough Haunts in a single covenant to form their own Warren, and such structures can be powerful forces for their faction\u2019s agenda or philosophy.<br /> <br /> <b>The Carthian Movement: </b>Firebrand Necropoli are communal hives, resembling guerrilla bases and underground resistance cells more than living spaces. With soapboxes on hand for whatever cause they\u2019re championing that night, a Carthian Warren\u2019s unity is a powerful weapon, though they often have trouble with the \u201csecret\u201d aspect, as their righteous anger struggles to contain itself to just one location.<br /> <br /> <b>The Circle of the Crone: </b>Warrens dedicated to the Crone are hellish, viscera-splattered caves with arcane totems marking the borders, promising a slow death to all intruders. Acolyte Necropoli form to consecrate territory to the Dark Mother, or to tear down something or someone that offends her. They\u2019re more primitive than other Necropoli, exploiting natural caverns and sinkholes, with dark altars where cultists can spill entrails to divine their deity\u2019s unholy will.<br /> <br /> <b>The Invictus:</b> Warrens sponsored by the First Estate often center around maintaining the Masquerade. Most are hubs where the Haunts can file away reports and coordinate enforcement, but some dedicate themselves to wetwork if the Invictus is on its back foot in the domain. In cities where the Conspiracy of Silence rules, a Warren might be the center of power, a hidden boardroom where the Inner Circle convenes to make the real decisions. These Necropoli are slick affairs, like oversized panic rooms covered in gleaming steel panels, stocked to the brim with the finer things in death. Hidden doesn\u2019t have to mean shabby.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lancea et Sanctum: </b>Sanctified Necropoli are underground temples where hooded priests read from the Testament by the light of flickering halogen bulbs, and warbling, hissing choruses sing out in supplication. These Warrens safeguard precious records or holy relics, but sometimes they\u2019re just meant to tighten the Judges\u2019 grip on a given area. The cores of these Warrens are always churches, but whether this means soaring arches lined with cracked stained glass, or spartan chambers and unadorned pews, depends on the sect.<br /> <br /> <b>The Ordo Dracul:</b> The Order is the least likely covenant to build Necropoli, as the unity of purpose they require is rare among the Defiant. When they do build them, however, Dragon Warrens are nightmare versions of scientific facilities, with lecture halls carved out of sewer brickwork, and rows of blood-stained labs where the cries of \u201cpatients\u201d echo for miles underground. Information gathering is the most obvious goal for these Necropoli, but a concerted effort to \u201cliberate\u201d a Wyrm\u2019s Nest could bring such Haunts together. A Warren built over a Nest develops all sorts of dangerous and esoteric features, any one of which might become the covenant\u2019s next breakthrough.<br /> <br /> <b>Pale Imitations</b><br /> <br /> Occasionally, one of the other clans tries its hand at an exclusive society. Such experiments never go on for very long \u2014 or end well \u2014 but they\u2019re horrifying and fascinating case studies while they last. The Haunts prefer to call them teachable moments.<br /> <br /> <b>Daeva Utopias:</b> When the Serpents gather together, the Vitae, alcohol, and sex flow like water, and screams of ecstasy drown out the cries of agony. Glittering monuments to excess and desire, Utopias tend to be cults of personality, with a single Daeva calling on other Serpents to share in his vision. Like fireworks, such places are beautiful, but fleeting. Jealousies flare, tempers rise, and appetites run rampant until the whole thing comes crashing down in glorious fashion.<br /> <br /> <b>Gangrel Freeholds: </b>It\u2019s rare for the independent Savages to try communal living, but it does happen from time to time. A family or coterie will carve out a swath of territory for their own, offering land and blood to any clanmate who wants to join up. It\u2019s a force to be reckoned with while it lasts; nobody wants to mess with a lone wolf, never mind a whole pack. That said, Gangrel aren\u2019t well known for accepting authority, and those who won\u2019t submit find it\u2019s easier just to move on. Freeholds often end with a whimper, not a bang, as members simply drift away.<br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue Kingdoms: </b>Sometimes, the Lords decide they need a place away from the petty squabbles of their inferiors, where the true elite of the All Night Society can gather to shape the fates of lesser beings. Ventrue Kingdoms always begin well, and are organized down to the stationary font \u2014 Ventrue love hierarchies, after all. Unfortunately, what they love more is power, and in a room full of CEOs, nobody wants to be the janitor. Kingdoms collapse under the weight of their subjects\u2019 egos, or grind to a halt as the struggle to be king overwhelms whatever purpose brought them together in the first place.<br /> <br /> <b>Mekhet [REDACTED]:</b> The Mekhet don\u2019t bother with such nonsense. Maybe they rent a meeting place, or maintain a bunker for emergencies, but only fools gather all together in one place. Much better to pull the strings from a distance, where no one even knows your name. For what the Shadows get up to when they do organize, see <b>Strange Shades: Mekhet</b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T13:58:18-08:00","id":1434699,"title":"","content":"I must say that I find it amusing that the Clans which have the greatest tendency to make Vampire Societies are the Nosferatu and the Julii (and the Mekhet, to a certain degree). Do you think that some of the other lesser/lost Clans (like the ones from Spilled Blood) may also have a potential to create a stable &quot;Kindred Society&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T15:27:31-08:00","id":1434703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1434699#post1434699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say that I find it amusing that the Clans which have the greatest tendency to make Vampire Societies are the Nosferatu and the Julii (and the Mekhet, to a certain degree). Do you think that some of the other lesser/lost Clans (like the ones from Spilled Blood) may also have a potential to create a stable &quot;Kindred Society&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good question. It's interesting, because that's often kind of the linking theme with lost clans. They try to create a cohesive society, and then they get burned for it. The Akhud, Amari, Nhang, and the Bekaak all follow that pattern in different ways (though with the Nhang they seem to have once been something different than vampires). The Hypatians would be an interesting case study, as their bane makes it difficult to remain in one place if they're not careful.<br /> <br /> I suppose the Twice-Cursed don't really fit into that, but they're not <i>quite </i>Kindred (in my headcanon).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T17:32:49-08:00","id":1434715,"title":"","content":"Well, we could always say that it is simply the nature of the Kindred to not get along with one another- it even makes sense, though we still have exceptions like the Nosferatu. And honestly the Julii, as they got along pretty well before the Strix decided to ruin everything....<br /> <br /> Well, the Nhang also got Strix possessed.<br /> <br /> And the Bekaak got cursed for eating a mummy.<br /> <br /> And the Amari got messed up by the global warming.<br /> <br /> And the Akhud got freaking destroyed by God.<br /> <br /> Ah. So every time that the Kindred manage to get along well and build a society of their own, it seems that some power in Heaven or Hell decides to say &quot;NOPE&quot; and bring them all back to square one. That makes you think, in that case, how the Nosferatu managed to avoid getting cursed in the same way so many other clans were ruined before. Maybe it is true- the Nosferatu are indeed more Damned than the rest of the Kindred, and they are already at rock bottom. They just can't fall any further. In a way, it is better to be dead than being a Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T21:28:10-08:00","id":1434730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431630-better-feared-nosferatu-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1433026#post1433026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Totally happy to answer questions!<br /> <br /> Theme-wise, my major note to the bloodline writers was to emphasize the horror. Some of the early drafts (and this included my own) were a tad too generic; they were good bloodlines, but not necessarily great <i>Nosferatu </i>bloodlines. The Gethsemeni, for instance, had a lot more emphasis on breaching the Masquerade in their first draft, whereas the final version focuses on the holy horror of being a prophet touched by the indefinable hand of God. All the bloodlines evince a different kind of scary: the unknown, knowing too much, being a cog in a machine, addiction and decadence, and so on.<br /> <br /> The ghoul families are more about the ways Nosferatu blood (for lack of a better term) fucks you up. Haunts have the most overt curse of the Damned, and that twisting nature can extend to their servants. Nosferatu ghouls are just <i>weirder </i>than those of other clans, and all of our ghoul families are a little off-kilter. For example, while we never come right out and say it, the Chamenos are really a subtype of ghoul rather than a family. We used the ghoul family mechanics for convenience, but they're more akin to things like mnemonic ghouls and Heisenbergs (both from <b>Half-Damned</b>). I've always liked the idea that Nosferatu ghouls mutate a bit, which is something you can find in <b>Masquerade </b>a bit more than <b>Requiem</b>, so that was the guiding light there.<br /> <br /> From a broader perspective, the overarching theme of the book was &amp;quot;Lonely Together&amp;quot;, and everything in <b>Better Feared </b>ties back to that. Nosferatu and their ghouls are insular rejects, so they had better get used to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the Gangrel mutate their ghouls a bit as well, their vitae is wild, chimerical, and just as weird as the Nosferatu Blood :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://foru